155
00:27:55,900 --> 00:27:58,059
thank you for the rigor, competence,

156
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:01,880
and high sense of judgments you bring to this assignment.

157
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:05,059
My particular thanks to Professor He Su Shin,

158
00:28:06,059 --> 00:28:09,720
whose contribution has been invaluable in bringing us

159
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:14,240
to this moment and establishing the Taiwan Independent CEDAW

160
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:17,680
Review model as an international template.

161
00:28:19,579 --> 00:28:23,019
Taiwan occupies a unique space in the international human

162
00:28:23,019 --> 00:28:24,099
rights landscape.

163
00:28:24,619 --> 00:28:27,079
As a non-United Nations member state,

164
00:28:27,359 --> 00:28:30,279
it cannot formally accede to CEDAW.

165
00:28:30,519 --> 00:28:34,319
Yet the Enforcement Act activated in 2011,

166
00:28:35,460 --> 00:28:38,240
Taiwan has voluntarily submitted itself

167
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:40,660
to the same rigor and accountability

168
00:28:40,660 --> 00:28:44,900
that binds 189 state parties around the world.

169
00:28:45,980 --> 00:28:48,700
Five national reports, five reviews,

170
00:28:49,099 --> 00:28:52,200
and decades of sustained good faith engagement

171
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:54,220
is what we see here.

172
00:28:54,680 --> 00:29:01,279
This historic CEDAW review and 25th Taiwan CEDAW

173
00:29:01,279 --> 00:29:05,500
anniversary celebration occurs as the committee marks

174
00:29:05,500 --> 00:29:08,839
45 years of the CEDAW ratification.

175
00:29:09,759 --> 00:29:12,099
Three things are evident in Taiwan.

176
00:29:13,259 --> 00:29:17,000
Commitment, consistency, and collaboration

177
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:20,920
within and among government as the duty bearer

178
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:23,740
and with stakeholders and rights holders.

179
00:29:25,180 --> 00:29:28,099
That commitment has not been rhetorical.

180
00:29:28,559 --> 00:29:32,200
Since the fourth review, Taiwan enacted the Stalking

181
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:35,920
and Harassment Prevention Act, amended the Gender Equality

182
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:40,079
in Employment Act, the Sexual Assault Crime Prevention Act,

183
00:29:40,420 --> 00:29:43,039
and the Domestic Violence Prevention Act,

184
00:29:44,079 --> 00:29:47,500
including establishing a sexual image processing

185
00:29:47,500 --> 00:29:50,619
center for non-consensual image abuse,

186
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:53,539
and many other actions that have been

187
00:29:53,539 --> 00:29:57,160
undertaken by the government.

188
00:29:57,160 --> 00:30:03,440
Some three 36,205 laws were screened for CEDAW compliance

189
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:09,839
with 244 out of 272 non-compliant instruments

190
00:30:09,839 --> 00:30:11,579
already amended.

191
00:30:12,359 --> 00:30:15,720
Today, over 41% of the legislative yuan

192
00:30:15,720 --> 00:30:20,200
is comprised of women, the highest proportion in Asia

193
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:24,980
that is worth commendation as it reflects a clear progressive

194
00:30:24,980 --> 00:30:31,019
step towards CEDAW GR40 standard of parity 50-50

195
00:30:31,019 --> 00:30:33,420
in leadership and governance.

196
00:30:34,279 --> 00:30:36,420
However, challenges persist.

197
00:30:37,220 --> 00:30:39,420
As the UN Human Rights Council noted,

198
00:30:39,940 --> 00:30:42,700
no country globally has achieved equality.

199
00:30:43,359 --> 00:30:45,440
And the UN Secretary General has warned

200
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:49,039
that achieving full global gender equality

201
00:30:49,039 --> 00:30:53,420
may take about 300 years, with women's rights being threatened

202
00:30:53,420 --> 00:30:56,579
and rolled back, especially in the digital world

203
00:30:56,579 --> 00:30:58,599
of technology and AI.

204
00:30:59,539 --> 00:31:02,420
At the Geneva Global Dialogue on AI Governance,

205
00:31:02,460 --> 00:31:04,779
which I had the privilege to attend this week,

206
00:31:05,460 --> 00:31:08,380
it was unequivocally agreed that there

207
00:31:08,380 --> 00:31:11,059
can be no true human rights-based AI

208
00:31:11,059 --> 00:31:14,779
governance in the world without the full implementation

209
00:31:14,779 --> 00:31:16,480
of CEDAW.

210
00:31:16,599 --> 00:31:19,359
Taiwan, as the undisputed backbone

211
00:31:19,359 --> 00:31:23,339
of the global digital hardware and semiconductor industry,

212
00:31:23,759 --> 00:31:27,640
has a unique role to play in modeling

213
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:31,180
inclusive digital governance and CEDAW accountability

214
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:33,839
across the technology value chain.

215
00:31:34,539 --> 00:31:38,059
Yet women hold only 12% of management positions

216
00:31:38,059 --> 00:31:42,299
of companies powering the semiconductor industry that

217
00:31:42,299 --> 00:31:45,799
produces more than 60% of the world's chips,

218
00:31:45,799 --> 00:31:49,700
despite being 37% of its workforce.

219
00:31:50,559 --> 00:31:55,779
Gender pay gap that was 15.8% in 2024 is widening.

220
00:31:55,880 --> 00:32:01,480
And over 250,000 migrant women sustaining the care economy

221
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:05,599
through Care for Taiwan's children, elderly, disabled,

222
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:09,319
and overall productivity human power base

223
00:32:09,319 --> 00:32:12,880
remain excluded from the Labor Standards Act

224
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:17,460
with no minimum wage, no overtime, no rest day.

225
00:32:18,380 --> 00:32:20,460
This structural exclusion sitting

226
00:32:20,460 --> 00:32:23,839
at the center of one of the world's most advanced

227
00:32:23,839 --> 00:32:28,240
digital economies reflects concerns usually perceived

228
00:32:28,240 --> 00:32:33,839
in Taiwan and everywhere, gaps in cascading, customization,

229
00:32:34,460 --> 00:32:40,920
and coordination of efforts that aim to embed and sustain

230
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:45,440
the pipeline required to achieve the safe, secure,

231
00:32:45,779 --> 00:32:48,759
sustainable, and inclusive future we all want.

232
00:32:49,519 --> 00:32:53,279
A realization that CEDAW matters beyond protection alone

233
00:32:53,279 --> 00:32:55,960
or addressing symptoms of inequality

234
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:58,400
like gender-based violence is needed.

235
00:32:59,059 --> 00:33:02,279
That CEDAW is an instrument for propagating

236
00:33:02,279 --> 00:33:04,339
the productivity of humanity.

237
00:33:04,980 --> 00:33:07,619
Every woman excluded from economic life,

238
00:33:07,619 --> 00:33:11,940
from leadership, from safety online, in the workplace,

239
00:33:12,299 --> 00:33:15,819
or at home is a loss not only to her personality,

240
00:33:16,279 --> 00:33:18,920
but to her society's productive capacity.

241
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:22,000
Equality is not a cost Taiwan bears.

242
00:33:22,579 --> 00:33:25,980
It is a multiplier not yet fully unlocked.

243
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:29,339
And the city's CEDAW model envisaged

244
00:33:29,339 --> 00:33:32,819
through the city of Taoyuan exchange visit

245
00:33:32,819 --> 00:33:37,200
is an opportunity to link Taiwan

246
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:39,720
with the city's CEDAW global coalition

247
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:42,119
now spanning many regions of the world.

248
00:33:42,680 --> 00:33:45,700
I hope this exchange bears fruitful seeds.

249
00:33:46,599 --> 00:33:50,740
Government makes laws, but women leave the reality of equality

250
00:33:50,740 --> 00:33:53,720
or exclusion at the level of the city

251
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:56,119
