Okay, so now articles one and two Marion will give you the floor.

1464
04:16:29,159 --> 04:16:32,719
Madam Chair, distinguished members of the delegation of Taiwan.

1465
04:16:32,719 --> 04:16:40,600
I warmly welcome all of us here today to this fifth independent review under the UN CEDAW convention.

1466
04:16:41,200 --> 04:16:50,059
And I thank the state party for its comprehensive report, its replies and for the constructive engagement that has characterized this review process.

1467
04:16:50,739 --> 04:16:56,379
I also wish to acknowledge the valuable contributions made by civil society organizations,

1468
04:16:56,379 --> 04:17:07,159
the National Human Rights Commission and other stakeholders whose submissions have enriched the committee's understanding of the progress achieved and the challenges that remain.

1469
04:17:08,520 --> 04:17:14,079
Taiwan has continued to demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing gender equality.

1470
04:17:14,719 --> 04:17:23,659
Since the previous review, the committee notes a number of important developments, including the continued implementation of the CEDAW Enforcement Act,

1471
04:17:23,659 --> 04:17:28,639
the systematic review of legislation for compliance with the convention,

1472
04:17:29,299 --> 04:17:33,780
the ongoing preparation of comprehensive anti-discrimination legislation,

1473
04:17:34,239 --> 04:17:40,299
and efforts to strengthen the application of the convention by judges, prosecutors and legal professionals.

1474
04:17:40,940 --> 04:17:47,299
These developments provide an important foundation for the realization of substantive equality for all women.

1475
04:17:47,299 --> 04:17:55,579
At the same time, the committee considers that several structural issues identified during previous reviews remain unresolved.

1476
04:17:56,100 --> 04:17:59,840
I will focus my intervention on articles one and two of the convention.

1477
04:18:01,520 --> 04:18:07,239
The committee welcomes the incorporation of the convention into domestic law through the CEDAW Enforcement Act,

1478
04:18:07,540 --> 04:18:13,000
which represents an important milestone in strengthening the domestic legal status of women's rights.

1479
04:18:13,000 --> 04:18:19,659
We also welcome the government's efforts to review legal legislation for consistency with the convention.

1480
04:18:20,459 --> 04:18:26,920
Nevertheless, the committee notes that concerns raised during previous reviews remain only partially addressed.

1481
04:18:27,700 --> 04:18:35,319
While the convention has domestic legal effect, it remains unclear whether institutional mechanisms have been fully established

1482
04:18:35,319 --> 04:18:40,100
to ensure its consistent implementation across all branches of government.

1483
04:18:40,100 --> 04:18:48,340
In particular, the committee notes the recommendation made in 2022 to establish a permanent parliamentary mechanism

1484
04:18:48,340 --> 04:18:52,040
to review legislation for compliance with the CEDAW,

1485
04:18:52,600 --> 04:18:59,979
as well as an appropriate complaints procedure for violation of women's human rights under the convention, have not materialized.

1486
04:19:00,719 --> 04:19:05,219
Please update the committee on the implementation of these recommendations.

1487
04:19:05,219 --> 04:19:10,220
What measures have been taken to establish a permanent mechanism to review legislation

1488
04:19:10,860 --> 04:19:15,799
and receive complaints concerning violations of rights protected under the convention?

1489
04:19:17,120 --> 04:19:22,559
The committee also welcomes the ongoing development of comprehensive anti-discrimination legislation.

1490
04:19:23,040 --> 04:19:28,559
We appreciate that consultations are currently taking place with a wide range of stakeholders.

1491
04:19:29,059 --> 04:19:33,220
However, we note that this process is now being under discussion for several years.

1492
04:19:33,540 --> 04:19:41,139
Can the delegation indicate the current status of the drafting process, the expected timeline for adoption,

1493
04:19:41,500 --> 04:19:48,299
and how it intends to ensure that the anti-discrimination legislation fully reflects Article 1 of the convention,

1494
04:19:48,879 --> 04:19:54,500
including a definition of discrimination encompassing direct and indirect discrimination,

1495
04:19:55,120 --> 04:20:00,540
multiple and intersecting forms of discrimination, and discrimination by both public and private actors?

1496
04:20:00,860 --> 04:20:10,600
Finally, under Article 1, the committee recalls that constitutional guarantees constitute the cornerstone of substantive equality.

1497
04:20:11,139 --> 04:20:16,700
Please explain whether consideration is being given to strengthening the constitutional framework

1498
04:20:16,700 --> 04:20:21,219
to include an explicit prohibition of discrimination against women

1499
04:20:21,219 --> 04:20:28,139
and a constitutional guarantee of substantive equality fully consistent with Articles 1 and 2 of the convention.

1500
04:20:28,139 --> 04:20:31,680
I now turn to the National Human Rights Institution.

1501
04:20:32,200 --> 04:20:35,559
The committee welcomes the establishment of the National Human Rights Commission

1502
04:20:35,559 --> 04:20:41,819
and notes the measures reportedly undertaken to strengthen its role in the protection of human rights.

1503
04:20:42,319 --> 04:20:48,959
However, during the previous review, the committee expressed concern regarding its operational independence,

1504
04:20:49,719 --> 04:20:53,760
particularly given its institutional placement within the Control Yuan,

1505
04:20:53,760 --> 04:20:58,760
and recommended that the Commission strengthen its independent complaints procedure

1506
04:20:59,299 --> 04:21:02,559
and seek accreditation under the Paris Principles.

1507
04:21:03,159 --> 04:21:04,860
And so my questions are the following.

1508
04:21:05,239 --> 04:21:09,719
Can you please update the Committee on Progress Made in implementing these recommendations?

1509
04:21:10,200 --> 04:21:17,920
In particular, how is the independence of the National Human Rights Commission guaranteed in law and in practice?

1510
04:21:17,920 --> 04:21:26,360
I know that the NHRC does not possess the power to compel public or private sectors to cooperate with investigations,

1511
04:21:27,059 --> 04:21:30,879
cease discriminatory conduct, or directly provide remedies.

1512
04:21:31,479 --> 04:21:37,399
How do you propose addressing this lack of competency in regard to the NHRC?

1513
04:21:38,500 --> 04:21:42,299
What progress has been made towards accreditation under the Paris Principles?

1514
04:21:42,299 --> 04:21:47,319
And how does the Commission's mandate differ from that of the Control Yuan

1515
04:21:47,319 --> 04:21:52,399
with regard to the protection of women's human rights and the handling of individual complaints?

1516
04:21:54,020 --> 04:21:56,719
In regard to access to justice and the remedies,

1517
04:21:57,180 --> 04:22:03,659
the committee welcomes the recent efforts to strengthen complaint procedures under the Sexual Harassment Prevention Act,

1518
04:22:04,079 --> 04:22:08,420
the Gender Equality and Employment Act, and the Gender Equity Education Act.

1519
04:22:08,420 --> 04:22:12,959
These reforms represent important progress in specific sectors.

1520
04:22:13,479 --> 04:22:19,959
Nevertheless, it remains unclear whether women whose rights are violated outside these legislative frameworks

1521
04:22:19,959 --> 04:22:25,639
have access to a comprehensive and coordinated system of remedies under the Convention.

1522
04:22:26,719 --> 04:22:31,020
Can the delegation update the Committee on what mechanisms currently exist

1523
04:22:31,020 --> 04:22:37,219
for women seeking redress for violations of their rights beyond these sector-specific laws?

1524
04:22:37,219 --> 04:22:46,700
In particular, how do mechanisms such as the Executive Yuan Gender Equality Complaint Mailbox operate in practice?

1525
04:22:47,479 --> 04:22:49,260
What remedies can they provide?

1526
04:22:49,639 --> 04:22:55,420
And is the Government considering the establishment of a comprehensive cross-sector complaints mechanism

1527
04:22:55,420 --> 04:22:59,220
capable of addressing violations of women's rights under the Convention,

1528
04:23:00,319 --> 04:23:02,840
including intersecting forms of discrimination?

1529
04:23:03,959 --> 04:23:06,079
I now look at the LBTI women.

1530
04:23:06,079 --> 04:23:12,819
The Committee welcomes Taiwan's significant advances in promoting equality, including marriage equality,

1531
04:23:13,239 --> 04:23:17,479
and the ongoing development of comprehensive anti-discrimination legislation.

1532
04:23:18,159 --> 04:23:20,959
These achievements have been recognized internationally.

1533
04:23:21,520 --> 04:23:30,059
At the same time, important protection gaps remain, particularly for transgender, intersex, and other gender diverse persons.

1534
04:23:30,059 --> 04:23:36,059
Can the delegation clarify whether the proposed comprehensive anti-discrimination legislation

1535
04:23:36,700 --> 04:23:45,000
will explicitly prohibit discrimination on the grounds of sexual orientation, gender identity, and sex characteristics?

1536
04:23:45,799 --> 04:23:50,059
Furthermore, what steps are being taken to establish a comprehensive legal framework

1537
04:23:50,579 --> 04:23:54,799
for legal gender recognition based on human rights principles,

1538
04:23:54,799 --> 04:24:00,600
including the elimination of disproportionate medical or psychiatric requirements,

1539
04:24:01,059 --> 04:24:08,079
and to review the binary household registration system so that it reflects the diversity of gender identities.

1540
04:24:10,079 --> 04:24:13,780
In regard to the application of the Convention by domestic courts,

1541
04:24:14,219 --> 04:24:19,979
the Committee welcomes the considerable efforts taken by the Judicial Yuan, the Ministry of Justice,

1542
04:24:19,979 --> 04:24:25,420
and other institutions to strengthen the application of the Convention within the judiciary.

1543
04:24:26,180 --> 04:24:31,959
The inclusion of CEDAW in mandatory judicial training, the development of a reference manual for judges,

1544
04:24:32,299 --> 04:24:39,899
specialized training programs, and the incorporation of the Convention into legal education all represent significant progress.

1545
04:24:40,399 --> 04:24:47,299
However, it remains uncertain whether these initiatives have resulted in the systematic application of the Convention

1546
04:24:47,299 --> 04:24:51,639
by domestic courts or whether they have become fully institutionalized.

1547
04:24:52,120 --> 04:25:00,219
And so in conclusion, I ask, can you please indicate what mechanisms are in place to monitor the practical impact of these initiatives?

1548
04:25:00,739 --> 04:25:04,639
Can you provide data on judicial decisions invoking the Convention

1549
04:25:04,639 --> 04:25:11,819
and explain whether consideration is being given to embedding these measures within binding legal or regulatory frameworks?

1550
04:25:11,819 --> 04:25:17,500
The Committee would also welcome information on measures being taken to establish a transparent

1551
04:25:17,500 --> 04:25:24,819
and effective internal grievance mechanism within the judiciary to address allegations of gender discrimination.

1552
04:25:25,399 --> 04:25:26,760
I thank you, Madam Chair.

1553
04:25:29,819 --> 04:25:30,540
Thank you very much.

1554
04:25:30,659 --> 04:25:36,120
I will now yield to the delegation for your responses to those questions.

1555
04:25:36,299 --> 04:25:37,139
Thank you.

1556
04:25:42,720 --> 04:25:48,760
Thank you very much for the questions.

1557
04:25:49,219 --> 04:25:52,000
So there are so many questions to address right now.

1558
04:25:52,260 --> 04:26:00,319
So I would like to ask our corresponding colleagues to answer these questions briefly.

1559
04:26:00,739 --> 04:26:07,440
So the enforcement law of CEDAW, about that, I would like to ask the Gender Equality Department to answer that.

1560
