1592
04:30:44,379 --> 04:30:55,040
These are all cases that we take on to ask and consult individuals, but that's a supplementary work that we do.

1593
04:30:55,260 --> 04:31:00,640
We are not following up for the EY. We're just repeating the things that we should do.

1594
04:31:02,250 --> 04:31:04,950
Is Judicial Yuan ready? Okay.

1595
04:31:06,530 --> 04:31:09,750
This is the Judicial Yuan. I am Judge Guo Yaoming.

1596
04:31:10,110 --> 04:31:11,889
Thank you very much for your questions.

1597
04:31:11,889 --> 04:31:22,329
For the substantial equality guarantee and protection, it's applied for in our Constitution,

1598
04:31:22,729 --> 04:31:35,290
and we use Constitution to make rulings that are not against substantial equality.

1599
04:31:35,290 --> 04:31:45,450
And for following that in the protection of female victims that are under GBV,

1600
04:31:45,829 --> 04:31:53,969
according to our response list, item 74 under page 7, page 3, page 74,

1601
04:31:54,510 --> 04:31:58,670
you are going to see that we've already explained it.

1602
04:31:58,670 --> 04:32:08,950
We provide quarantine or protective measures, including remote consultation and recovery measures.

1603
04:32:09,250 --> 04:32:16,090
We also make sure that we provide protective measures to victims of domestic violence,

1604
04:32:16,170 --> 04:32:21,809
and we ask about their safety requirements before the hearing.

1605
04:32:22,729 --> 04:32:27,549
We make sure that we take care of the victims' safety requirements.

1606
04:32:27,549 --> 04:32:32,190
For example, they use a discrete channel, and they're accompanied by the social workers.

1607
04:32:33,030 --> 04:32:35,329
And these cases cannot be mediated.

1608
04:32:35,790 --> 04:32:44,430
For other cases that do implicate domestic violence,

1609
04:32:45,030 --> 04:32:53,270
we have mediators and commissioners that have expertise in domestic violence.

1610
04:32:53,270 --> 04:33:00,930
For the administrative part, we conduct training for CEDAW every year

1611
04:33:00,930 --> 04:33:05,430
for new judges and all the on-the-job judges and all of the staff.

1612
04:33:05,990 --> 04:33:14,290
Whether or not the judges and the courts cite CEDAW according to the Convention,

1613
04:33:14,830 --> 04:33:19,869
it depends on the courts and their individual judges.

1614
04:33:19,869 --> 04:33:26,650
It's not us from the Jiu Jiu Shou Yuan that can decide whether or not we intervene.

1615
04:33:26,830 --> 04:33:30,029
And now we give the floor to the Human Rights Department.

1616
04:33:31,850 --> 04:33:39,849
I am Director of the Department of Human Rights and Transitional Justice.

1617
04:33:40,529 --> 04:33:46,689
Regarding the Anti-Discrimination Act progress, in 2024,

1618
04:33:46,689 --> 04:33:53,909
the EY published the Draft on Anti-Discrimination Act.

1619
04:33:54,650 --> 04:34:03,049
And over the two years, we've continued inviting the NHRC, EY, and relevant authorities,

1620
04:34:04,349 --> 04:34:10,689
metropolitan governments, and Department of Gender Equality to consult various stakeholders

1621
04:34:10,990 --> 04:34:16,810
and to clarify all of the conflicts in the draft.

1622
04:34:17,409 --> 04:34:28,310
We have recently held two review meetings, especially when it involves the public

1623
04:34:28,310 --> 04:34:33,729
and the transactions, and it could implicate the general life.

1624
04:34:34,470 --> 04:34:37,950
So we need to strike a balance between protecting the people

1625
04:34:37,950 --> 04:34:40,470
and also protecting the freedom of religion.

1626
04:34:41,110 --> 04:34:49,549
So this is something we need to further discuss and to discuss with the stakeholders.

1627
04:34:50,110 --> 04:34:53,790
And secondly, regarding the definition and scope of discrimination,

1628
04:34:54,509 --> 04:35:00,529
in Anti-Discrimination Act, we refer to CRPD number six, general opinion,

1629
04:35:00,529 --> 04:35:11,830
and it is specified that this definition of discrimination is discriminatory treatment

1630
04:35:11,830 --> 04:35:21,549
or different treatment, direct discrimination, indirect discrimination,

1631
04:35:21,869 --> 04:35:26,250
and refuse to adjust, and so on, as definitions for discrimination.

1632
04:35:26,250 --> 04:35:32,790
And the scope covers all of the race, skin color, the sources, or mother country,

1633
04:35:33,229 --> 04:35:42,549
indigenous peoples, gender, gender orientation, sexual orientation, disability, age, religion, and so on.

1634
04:35:43,250 --> 04:35:51,849
In referring to the international conventions, we also look at the domains that fit the public need in Taiwan.

1635
04:35:51,849 --> 04:35:59,069
And we focus on employment and education where discrimination and differential treatment may happen,

1636
04:35:59,389 --> 04:36:03,689
and this is a follow-up to the question that was proposed.

1637
04:36:04,270 --> 04:36:05,290
Thank you very much.

1638
04:36:05,610 --> 04:36:14,450
Now we further ask from Control Yuan, the NHRC, to talk about the operations of NHRC.

1639
04:36:14,990 --> 04:36:20,490
Hello. I am the vice chairperson of NHRC.

1640
04:36:20,490 --> 04:36:27,909
Here I would like to assure that the international reviewers indeed have pointed out

1641
04:36:27,909 --> 04:36:34,729
there is a limit to our independence operating as the NHRC

1642
04:36:34,729 --> 04:36:42,569
because we were established as a dual hat for the Control Yuan commissioners.

1643
04:36:42,590 --> 04:36:49,490
So we have seven Control Yuan commissioners who are also working as NHRC commissioners.

1644
04:36:49,819 --> 04:36:56,220
Over these past six years, we've noticed that there is a limit, and we need to break through this.

1645
04:36:56,400 --> 04:37:06,060
We will be relieved from office this July, and we've also suggested that amendments must be made.

1646
04:37:06,319 --> 04:37:15,840
But it's very difficult at LY because the LY has already been calling out for the abolishment of Control Yuan.

1647
04:37:15,840 --> 04:37:27,979
If that happens, the NHRC will be demolished altogether, and there will be no commissioners for review.

1648
04:37:28,319 --> 04:37:34,099
That's what we're worried about, so we need to amend the Organization Act for NHRC.

1649
04:37:34,860 --> 04:37:42,080
Of course, we don't even have the enactment code for NHRC staff.

1650
04:37:42,080 --> 04:37:49,299
These are all limitations that we're facing, so we hope that all political parties,

1651
04:37:49,759 --> 04:37:54,099
when they're discussing about the abolishment of Control Yuan,

1652
04:37:54,639 --> 04:38:00,200
they should treat NHRC individually and establish one individually.

1653
04:38:01,439 --> 04:38:05,080
That's a very important recommendation from us. Thank you. Thank you very much.

1654
04:38:05,619 --> 04:38:10,060
Is the Department of Gender Equality going to answer about complaints?

1655
04:38:11,659 --> 04:38:20,380
Regarding the cross-department complaints filing, we have also responded in our list.

1656
04:38:21,000 --> 04:38:31,419
We have a Gender Equality mailbox for the general public,

1657
04:38:31,900 --> 04:38:36,380
and if there are any issues regarding this, they can write to this mailbox.

1658
04:38:36,380 --> 04:38:40,099
It's a cross-department mechanism.

1659
04:38:40,880 --> 04:38:48,439
Once the public file a complaint to this mailbox, the Department of Gender Equality will review it.

1660
04:38:48,779 --> 04:38:56,000
If it involves certain regulations or administrative measures, or if it's an individual item,

1661
04:38:56,000 --> 04:39:05,900
we will ask the Compton Authority to clarify this and provide substantial administrative guidance.

1662
04:39:08,159 --> 04:39:16,159
If the review confirms a violation of CEDAW, the Compton Ministry or agency is required to amend

1663
04:39:16,159 --> 04:39:18,580
or repeal the relevant provisions.

1664
04:39:18,939 --> 04:39:24,180
Such cases are subsequently incorporated into CEDAW follow-up monitoring and control mechanisms.

1665
04:39:24,180 --> 04:39:32,659
In the future, we will continue to reinforce the negotiations across departments

1666
04:39:32,659 --> 04:39:38,459
and to follow up and to regularly review the complaints from the public

1667
04:39:38,459 --> 04:39:42,580
and all the complaints that are made for CEDAW.

1668
04:39:43,099 --> 04:39:49,259
We will further control this and also further implement CEDAW. Thank you very much.

1669
04:39:49,259 --> 04:39:52,520
Now we've heard from various agencies.

1670
04:39:53,439 --> 04:39:59,279
We would like to know if anyone would like to follow up on your answers

1671
04:39:59,279 --> 04:40:05,599
or if any other agencies or departments that I haven't called up on would like to follow up.

1672
04:40:05,880 --> 04:40:07,459
Feel free to take the floor now.

1673
04:40:07,680 --> 04:40:10,139
For example, Judicial Yuan, you have spoken.

1674
04:40:11,139 --> 04:40:22,479
Department of Human Rights, you did not talk about diversification of genders.

1675
04:40:23,220 --> 04:40:30,520
Yes, we talked about discrimination includes gender and gender orientation and gender traits,

1676
04:40:30,619 --> 04:40:32,779
so I think that covers the diversification.

1677
04:40:33,380 --> 04:40:35,040
What about NHRC?

1678
04:40:35,040 --> 04:40:38,900
Did you talk about individual complaints?

1679
04:40:41,560 --> 04:40:45,419
Do you have anything to follow up on?

1680
04:40:47,340 --> 04:40:48,979
I don't think so.

1681
04:40:50,419 --> 04:40:59,419
If no other follow-ups, we would like to give the floor back to our reviewers for further questions.

1682
04:40:59,479 --> 04:41:00,259
Thank you.

1683
04:41:01,279 --> 04:41:06,840
Thank you very much for the comprehensive responses from the different arms,

1684
04:41:07,240 --> 04:41:14,840
but I think we still need clarity on some areas, and I'll turn the floor to Niklas. Thank you.

1685
04:41:14,959 --> 04:41:20,000
Thank you very much for the answers provided.

1686
04:41:20,380 --> 04:41:27,319
I still want to come back to the draft Anti-Discrimination Act

1687
04:41:27,319 --> 04:41:33,919
because this has been now on the agenda for a long time,

1688
04:41:34,340 --> 04:41:49,580
and I didn't understand, is there any clear timetable for the adoption and presentation of this Act for the Legislative Yuan?

1689
04:41:54,200 --> 04:42:01,860
The two review meetings are of course important, but how is this now going forward?

1690
04:42:02,360 --> 04:42:09,919
Is there a clear commitment from the side of the government to actually go forward with this project?

1691
04:42:10,099 --> 04:42:10,580
Thank you.

1692
04:42:13,620 --> 04:42:14,220
Marion?

1693
04:42:16,720 --> 04:42:23,319
Thank you very much, and I too thank the delegation for its responses to some of my questions.

1694
04:42:23,840 --> 04:42:30,400
There are two areas that I really want to look at and express my concern about the National Human Rights Commission

1695
04:42:30,400 --> 04:42:36,939
and the possible challenges to its very life and existence as you have put forward,

1696
04:42:36,939 --> 04:42:48,919
and I trust that Taiwan will move to the place where the NHRC is an independent, autonomous institution

1697
04:42:48,919 --> 04:42:53,060
based on the Paris Principles and moving forward.

1698
04:42:53,880 --> 04:42:57,639
I appreciate the challenges that you have put forward there.

1699
04:42:57,639 --> 04:43:06,319
The other issue is really Article 1 of the CEDAW Convention and the definition of discrimination

1700
04:43:06,319 --> 04:43:12,380
that is really vital and a pillar of the work that we're doing,

1701
04:43:12,759 --> 04:43:16,080
and I'm not hearing clearly, and correct me if I'm wrong,

1702
04:43:16,560 --> 04:43:26,259
that the definition as provided by CEDAW is their movement to incorporate that into the anti-discrimination legislation.

1703
04:43:26,259 --> 04:43:34,360
I heard one member of the delegation speak of the discrimination definition of the persons with disabilities.

1704
04:43:35,279 --> 04:43:36,400
That is well and good.

1705
04:43:36,720 --> 04:43:45,260
CEDAW also has a very comprehensive definition that is really important for gender substantive equality to take place,

1706
04:43:46,119 --> 04:43:50,259
for it to be incorporated into the anti-discrimination legislation.

1707
04:43:50,360 --> 04:43:52,919
So I'd like to hear a response to that.

1708
04:43:53,000 --> 04:43:53,880
Thank you.

1709
04:44:00,280 --> 04:44:02,119
Thank you.

1710
04:44:02,619 --> 04:44:13,700
So from our two IRC members' questions, we can actually see that they are very concerned about anti-discrimination act.

1711
04:44:14,700 --> 04:44:24,060
So the first member mentioned that very concrete timetable for the entire progress of adoption of anti-discrimination act,

1712
04:44:24,060 --> 04:44:28,840
and also the second member talked about the actual definition of discrimination,

1713
04:44:29,279 --> 04:44:35,119
so whether that is very specifically reflected in the anti-discrimination act.

1714
04:44:35,380 --> 04:44:40,159
So maybe we can ask the Department of Human Rights to add information,

1715
04:44:40,220 --> 04:44:45,200
and if the Department of Gender Equality would like to add on, please chip in later.

1716
04:44:45,240 --> 04:44:46,080
Thank you.

1717
04:44:47,439 --> 04:44:52,400
So this is Executive Yuan, Department of Human Rights and Transitional Justice.

1718
04:44:52,400 --> 04:45:00,599
This is my second time giving answers, so about the definition of discrimination in our first answer

1719
04:45:00,599 --> 04:45:08,680
that we focus on the discriminatory treatment according to CRPD and other international covenants,

1720
04:45:09,220 --> 04:45:14,159
international indirect definition of discrimination.

1721
04:45:14,360 --> 04:45:20,060
So for the first version and second version, we are going to focus on the definition of direct and indirect discrimination,

1722
04:45:20,060 --> 04:45:28,319
and also harassment, and also the rejection to providing reasonable accommodation for people with disabilities.

1723
04:45:28,680 --> 04:45:38,060
So these are the types highlighted by the definition, and in terms of the traits, including race and also ethnicity,

1724
04:45:38,799 --> 04:45:46,979
for example, ethnicity and skin color, and also gender expression, gender or sexual orientation,

1725
04:45:48,480 --> 04:45:51,599
age and religion, we have the five categories.

1726
04:45:51,659 --> 04:45:59,119
So these five traits will be covered by our draft to address this anti-discrimination act.

1727
04:45:59,540 --> 04:46:05,639
So these are the bases and then also the traits that we have identified.

1728
04:46:05,880 --> 04:46:07,060
Why the five ones?

1729
04:46:07,560 --> 04:46:11,740
And when it comes to the direction of anti-discrimination act,

1730
04:46:11,740 --> 04:46:22,020
we would like to see specific effectiveness for this discriminatory treatment and rejection of reasonable accommodation.

1731
04:46:22,419 --> 04:46:25,720
This takes place in the daily life of our general public.

1732
04:46:25,880 --> 04:46:34,799
These people, they need to have face this civil rate, civil code liability, so it's legally binding.

1733
04:46:34,799 --> 04:46:44,180
That is why that the entire act apply scope and definition are quite specific,

1734
04:46:45,979 --> 04:46:55,119
because this act is a supplement to the anti-discrimination legal remediation framework.

1735
04:46:56,000 --> 04:46:59,020
So we would like to enhance that remediation.

1736
04:46:59,020 --> 04:47:09,020
And then also in the legislative statement, we actually highlighted multiple discrimination and intersectional discrimination.

1737
04:47:09,740 --> 04:47:10,799
Those are highlighted.

1738
04:47:11,340 --> 04:47:20,880
And then all the provisions, even though they do not provide the definition of multilayer discrimination and intersectional discrimination,

1739
04:47:20,880 --> 04:47:28,479
however, if they are actually several traits indicating discriminatory treatment,

1740
04:47:28,540 --> 04:47:33,680
that also constitutes the discrimination that is defined by this act.

1741
04:47:34,119 --> 04:47:37,659
So that is my answer to the first article of CITO,

1742
04:47:37,819 --> 04:47:42,919
whether the CITO's definition of discrimination is incorporated into the anti-discrimination act.

1743
04:47:43,259 --> 04:47:46,040
And then also in May, we have the two covenants review.

1744
04:47:46,040 --> 04:47:55,299
And also our civil society groups are very concerned about the timeline and timetable of these anti-discrimination acts.

1745
04:47:56,040 --> 04:48:04,779
Indeed, we started in 2024 that under the first national action plan of national human rights.

1746
04:48:05,540 --> 04:48:07,759
So we had two versions developed.

1747
04:48:08,080 --> 04:48:14,880
And then in during that two year time frame, that executive we are still on track.

1748
04:48:14,880 --> 04:48:26,459
We are still working on putting together and of these disputes and bringing up focuses.

1749
04:48:26,860 --> 04:48:28,979
And also these involves the public life.

1750
04:48:29,299 --> 04:48:34,380
So we work with government agencies to consult different industries.

1751
04:48:35,500 --> 04:48:42,319
And then also in the past issues, for example, the accessibility, indigenous issues, gender and religion issues,

1752
04:48:42,319 --> 04:48:51,439
we did have specific consultation hearings to take different opinions from scholars,

1753
04:48:51,700 --> 04:48:53,779
academia and industry players.

1754
04:48:54,159 --> 04:49:01,220
In addition to this general like commercial transactions, there are still disputes this morning.

1755
04:49:01,459 --> 04:49:05,700
I think that when it comes to hate speech, we had a discussion.

1756
04:49:05,700 --> 04:49:12,400
So I think both departments of human rights and also civil society group, we have different opinions on that.

1757
04:49:12,720 --> 04:49:16,200
So I think we should be very cautious in treating that dispute.

1758
04:49:17,099 --> 04:49:25,299
And in terms of timetable, we will work hard with the covenants reviews of two covenants and CEDAW.

1759
04:49:25,540 --> 04:49:32,819
We will still try to accelerate the adoption of this anti-discrimination act.

1760
04:49:32,819 --> 04:49:39,400
We don't have specific timetable, but we still need to take a comprehensive inventory of all the disputes.

1761
04:49:39,459 --> 04:49:41,279
That will be our focus for the time being.

1762
04:49:41,639 --> 04:49:47,340
So the Department of Gender Equality just told me that they don't have anything to add so far.

1763
04:49:47,639 --> 04:49:53,979
Do we have any other colleagues who would like to answer anti-discrimination act questions?

1764
04:49:54,220 --> 04:49:57,340
Any additional information you would like to provide?

1765
04:49:59,779 --> 04:50:01,540
If it seems none.

1766
04:50:01,540 --> 04:50:04,819
So I'm going to give the floor back to Madame Chair.

1767
04:50:05,040 --> 04:50:05,939
Thank you.

1768
04:50:09,819 --> 04:50:11,259
Thank you very much.

1769
04:50:11,459 --> 04:50:25,419
I think you have really elaborated, giving us insights on the timeline on certain parameters and work arrangements that are ongoing with the different arms of government,

1770
04:50:25,680 --> 04:50:29,840
with the Legislative Yuan, the Human Rights Commission, and the Minister of Justice.

1771
04:50:29,840 --> 04:50:31,340
And we appreciate that.

1772
04:50:31,700 --> 04:50:34,680
I think we will now move on to articles three and four.

1773
04:50:34,900 --> 04:50:40,119
And for this, I would like to pose some questions.

1774
04:50:41,099 --> 04:50:58,080
I really commend all of the efforts that have been outlined by the delegation in terms of implementation of a system wide process for delivering on gender equality.

1775
04:50:58,080 --> 04:51:04,380
A number of measures were identified in the response.

1776
04:51:04,979 --> 04:51:12,340
However, there are still areas that some additional clarification would be most appreciated.

1777
04:51:12,919 --> 04:51:17,200
And I will proceed to highlight some of these now.

1778
04:51:18,200 --> 04:51:20,459
In terms of data.

1779
04:51:22,979 --> 04:51:24,900
Give me just one minute.

1780
04:51:31,560 --> 04:51:32,159
Yes.

1781
04:51:33,819 --> 04:51:41,139
I would like to start with the standardization of the coordination mechanisms.

1782
04:51:41,639 --> 04:51:45,319
I know that a lot has been put in place.

1783
04:51:45,319 --> 04:51:56,939
You have performance indicators and you've been able to work out how to relate to other, with other departments.

1784
04:51:57,500 --> 04:52:09,020
However, most of the responses that we have about lateral and vertical oversight across the five branches of the government

1785
04:52:09,879 --> 04:52:16,099
in terms of dealing with accountability measures seem to speak to normative frameworks.

1786
04:52:16,159 --> 04:52:18,360
You're talking about the policies that you have.

1787
04:52:18,680 --> 04:52:21,020
You're talking about legislation that you have.

1788
04:52:21,400 --> 04:52:32,700
And I just wonder what kind of benchmarks for accountability and effectiveness have been placed, have been put in place.

1789
04:52:32,700 --> 04:52:42,819
Are there any quality assurance measures, any compliance indicators that you have been able to put in place?

1790
04:52:43,639 --> 04:52:50,819
Because the department already, you have the Enforcement Act, you have policies across all of the sectors.

1791
04:52:51,139 --> 04:52:57,099
But how do you ensure that these policies move from just policy to practice?

1792
04:52:57,920 --> 04:53:03,060
Do you have any clear mechanisms that you have put in place?

1793
04:53:03,139 --> 04:53:04,220
That's the first question.

1794
04:53:04,700 --> 04:53:14,919
The second is the report and your response says that you play a central role in integrating, supervising, and coordinating.

1795
04:53:15,900 --> 04:53:19,939
My question is how, how is this done?

1796
04:53:20,720 --> 04:53:24,080
Do you produce gap analysis reports?

1797
04:53:24,080 --> 04:53:29,880
Do you have a surveillance system that generates information on gaps?

1798
04:53:30,720 --> 04:53:36,720
Is there a periodic monitoring and assessment schedule or regimen in place?

1799
04:53:36,799 --> 04:53:40,759
Is this done quarterly, biannually, or biennially?

1800
04:53:41,259 --> 04:53:48,720
And I really would like to add to the question on follow-up that was asked earlier on.

1801
04:53:48,720 --> 04:53:55,520
As a coordinating entity, is there a systematized follow-up and appraisal mechanism?

1802
04:53:55,840 --> 04:53:59,380
And how does this operate in practice?

1803
04:54:00,560 --> 04:54:06,340
The third area I would like to focus on is on your guidance and incentive program,

1804
04:54:06,619 --> 04:54:14,900
which I think is very commendable for municipalities, counties, and city governments.

1805
04:54:14,900 --> 04:54:27,200
I know that that was enacted, but the question is how do you ensure that these incentive programs that are ongoing respond to specific local needs and priorities?

1806
04:54:27,540 --> 04:54:34,400
For instance, is there room for different localities to focus on different priorities?

1807
04:54:34,400 --> 04:54:44,840
Or is there a standard across the board priority that is a preset for different localities to respond to?

1808
04:54:45,220 --> 04:54:52,639
And if that is the case, and for whatever mechanism that has been in place, what has been the concrete outcome?

1809
04:54:53,520 --> 04:54:55,500
Has there been any policy reset?

1810
04:54:55,740 --> 04:55:01,599
Was there an area where the policy or the benchmark didn't work and you have had to redefine the policy?

1811
04:55:01,599 --> 04:55:05,959
Has there been any service reforms in any particular sector?

1812
04:55:06,340 --> 04:55:14,819
Because that would be an indication of how that your coordination mechanism is working in practice.

1813
04:55:15,720 --> 04:55:18,259
Then there is the issue of the follow-up.

1814
04:55:18,860 --> 04:55:21,939
I think the process was reportedly started.

1815
04:55:22,400 --> 04:55:24,680
I've asked the frequency of it.

1816
04:55:24,680 --> 04:55:31,380
I would like to know how often you engage with civil society, the private sector,

1817
04:55:31,680 --> 04:55:38,340
and other arms of government to ascertain progress towards the agreed targets and milestones.

1818
04:55:39,939 --> 04:55:49,959
And concerning the excellence performance, I know that a guidance mechanism was reportedly provided for underperformers,

1819
04:55:50,279 --> 04:55:53,740
while those with excellent performance were rewarded.

1820
04:55:53,740 --> 04:56:04,919
Can you provide information and data on beneficiaries of this excellence award since it was instituted in 2022?

1821
04:56:09,439 --> 04:56:16,340
On encouraging and guiding line ministries, ministries, departments, and agencies,

1822
04:56:16,619 --> 04:56:20,799
and the other arms of government with respects to your gender responsive budgeting,

1823
04:56:20,799 --> 04:56:30,279
could you indicate or provide information on any mandatory requirements or budget preconditions or parameters

1824
04:56:30,279 --> 04:56:38,900
that are used to assess the budget performance either prior to submitting to the Legislative Yuan for appropriation

1825
04:56:38,900 --> 04:56:42,220
or during the appropriation process?

1826
04:56:43,260 --> 04:56:50,880
And in the same vein, can you indicate how a default, how gender enforcement system,

1827
04:56:51,259 --> 04:56:53,459
how is the default mechanism working?

1828
04:56:53,580 --> 04:56:58,240
Those who do not meet the threshold that you have set as performance,

1829
04:56:58,520 --> 04:57:04,439
because you talk about excellence and underperformance, how is that dealt with?

1830
04:57:04,900 --> 04:57:09,439
How many numbers do you have data on the number of defaults in MDAs?

1831
04:57:09,439 --> 04:57:17,299
The penalties imposed, if any, or if there are any deterrent measures that would encourage ministries, departments,

1832
04:57:17,439 --> 04:57:23,979
or other arms of government to take the gender responsive budgeting more seriously in future budgets.

1833
04:57:25,080 --> 04:57:30,500
You also provided information on increased gender budgeting over the period,

1834
04:57:30,500 --> 04:57:41,360
moving from 134.6 billion in 2022 to 155.5 billion in 2023 and an increase in 2024.

1835
04:57:41,959 --> 04:57:47,479
But it appears that those budgets were mainly due to expansion of policies,

1836
04:57:47,779 --> 04:57:52,720
such as measures for declining birth rates and long-term care services.

1837
04:57:53,720 --> 04:58:03,939
Are there any compilation of gender budget expenditure across sectors beyond health and long-term care,

1838
04:58:04,720 --> 04:58:12,979
like in environment, in judiciary, in agriculture, infrastructure, roads, housing?

1839
04:58:13,340 --> 04:58:20,979
It would be interesting to know if there was a corresponding increase in budget in some of those departments,

1840
04:58:20,979 --> 04:58:26,500
because what you report seems to be basically on health and long-term care.

1841
04:58:28,060 --> 04:58:31,959
Also on the guidance, the gender equality guidance policy,

1842
04:58:32,840 --> 04:58:40,360
I'm curious to know what concrete results have been achieved on the application of this guidance or advisory policy.

1843
04:58:40,840 --> 04:58:46,340
Has there been significant transformation or substantive equality that you can attribute

1844
04:58:46,340 --> 04:58:52,080
to the application of those guidance measures in particular sectors?

1845
04:58:52,919 --> 04:59:02,439
And on the sectoral service delivery, how has the guidance measure, the policy guidance measure,

1846
04:59:02,740 --> 04:59:13,080
how has it impacted on core economic sectors, the financial sector, agriculture, environment, transportation?

1847
04:59:13,080 --> 04:59:17,220
Do you have any records in that respect?

1848
04:59:17,900 --> 04:59:21,000
I'm also curious about your local government.

1849
04:59:21,520 --> 04:59:30,659
I hear about the act that enables MDAs or policies to decentralize and go to the local areas.

1850
04:59:31,700 --> 04:59:38,439
Could you give concrete examples of which local governments have actually been able to uptake on those laws,

1851
04:59:38,439 --> 04:59:50,759
their priority focus, the reach and the outcomes of the interventions or programs that have been packaged by those local governments?

1852
04:59:51,360 --> 04:59:57,639
And with regards to the gender equality committees, specialized teams that meet regularly,

1853
04:59:58,139 --> 05:00:05,520
do you have any details of the tracking, the reports that were found by those gender equality committees?

1854
05:00:05,520 --> 05:00:11,880
What improvement plans, progress and benchmarks have been agreed by those committees?

1855
05:00:12,400 --> 05:00:14,040
And how would you rate progress?

1856
05:00:14,200 --> 05:00:17,419
What parameters are you using to rate progress?

1857
05:00:17,759 --> 05:00:20,259
Is it poor, fair, good, excellent?

1858
05:00:20,900 --> 05:00:24,360
It would be useful or interesting to know.

1859
05:00:24,860 --> 05:00:31,259
And I mentioned about the Excellence Award and in particular the Golden Carnation Awards

1860
05:00:31,259 --> 05:00:35,959
and Spotlight, which has been spotlighted as models for other agencies.

1861
05:00:36,439 --> 05:00:42,560
Please indicate the number of excellent gender performers that have been recorded,

1862
05:00:42,639 --> 05:00:48,360
those that have been awarded the Golden Carnation or Spotlight model since 2022.

1863
05:00:48,779 --> 05:00:54,260
And for the underperformers, are you able to share the list of underperforming MDAs?

1864
05:00:55,000 --> 05:00:57,060
I would like to stop there for now. Thank you.

1865
05:01:11,299 --> 05:01:27,720
Thank you very much for your questions, whether it's in regarding the horizontal or vertical implementations

1866
05:01:27,720 --> 05:01:35,740
or any concrete examples for the locals and also budgeting for the gender equality.

1867
05:01:36,200 --> 05:01:42,459
These are for the Department of Gender Equality, so I'm going to give the floor to the Department of Gender Equality.

1868
05:01:54,700 --> 05:02:00,400
This is the Department of Gender Equality, and I'm Section Chief Zhang.

1869
05:02:02,459 --> 05:02:11,360
Regarding your questions, how do we have a systematic mechanism to know about the gap?

1870
05:02:11,360 --> 05:02:13,419
How do we have a gap analysis?

1871
05:02:15,659 --> 05:02:24,479
We have a gender equality guideline policy, and every four years we look at the statistics and the gaps

1872
05:02:24,479 --> 05:02:31,139
and the discrepancies and discuss with all of our committee members and CSO members,

1873
05:02:31,500 --> 05:02:37,000
private sector members to discuss certain gender issues that we need to work on and improve.

1874
05:02:37,000 --> 05:02:52,000
And in these plans, every year, regularly, we have a meeting at the EY gender equality meeting,

1875
05:02:52,880 --> 05:02:55,319
and we talk about our implementations.

1876
05:02:55,319 --> 05:03:09,439
Most of the commissioners of our gender equality commission at L.Y. are CSOs and civil society experts,

1877
05:03:09,700 --> 05:03:16,139
and they provide us with their opinions on how do we promote and improve gender equality,

1878
05:03:16,200 --> 05:03:21,759
and we also work with the private sectors to talk about how we can further facilitate,

1879
05:03:21,759 --> 05:03:29,599
and we also accept proposals from the private sectors, and they come in for the meetings with the commissioners.

1880
05:03:30,020 --> 05:03:40,760
So the meetings are held regularly once a year, and the viewers also asked about our advisory mechanism

1881
05:03:41,619 --> 05:03:48,760
for how do we incentivize them, intensive reward them if they're performing well,

1882
05:03:49,169 --> 05:03:52,450
and what do we do for those underperformers.

1883
05:03:52,729 --> 05:04:08,090
Every two years, we have a performance review, and all of these performance reviews are on a rolling management mechanism,

1884
05:04:08,090 --> 05:04:17,889
which also includes opinions from our CSO representatives and experts and scholars,

1885
05:04:18,150 --> 05:04:22,430
and they provide consultation to local government or central government,

1886
05:04:22,689 --> 05:04:31,090
and for those that perform well, we provide them a reward, whether it's an award or bonus,

1887
05:04:32,130 --> 05:04:37,310
and it's provided, it's awarded by the premier, and for underperformers,

1888
05:04:37,729 --> 05:04:52,250
we provide further guidance, and following the civil service, civil society commissioners' suggestion,

1889
05:04:52,650 --> 05:04:55,069
we also follow in for improvement.

1890
05:04:56,069 --> 05:05:03,290
Hello, I'm from the Department of Gender Equality, and for the tool of budgeting,

1891
05:05:04,029 --> 05:05:11,529
starting from 2020, we started implementing the gender budget,

1892
05:05:11,930 --> 05:05:20,389
and all of the organizations and agencies are asked to budget for gender issues,

1893
05:05:21,910 --> 05:05:27,330
which replaces the mid- and long-term projects we've had in the future,

1894
05:05:27,509 --> 05:05:33,990
and we also discuss and follow up, and to look at how they execute all of these budgets,

1895
05:05:34,569 --> 05:05:44,750
and we discuss it with our external experts to make sure that the investment we make is consistent with our gender goals,

1896
05:05:44,750 --> 05:05:54,869
and in 2022 to 2025, gender equality promotion program also has a budget,

1897
05:05:55,810 --> 05:06:09,729
also had a budget that worked with the KPIs so that they align with our budgets and our substantial and concrete policies.

1898
05:06:10,810 --> 05:06:20,369
At Executive Yuan, we also look at their final results for the use of the gender budgets,

1899
05:06:20,590 --> 05:06:28,069
and if necessary, we will revise accordingly and revise our principles,

1900
05:06:28,569 --> 05:06:35,529
and to see if there are any items that are underperforming, we ask for further monitoring,

1901
05:06:35,529 --> 05:06:51,930
and the viewer also mentioned whether we have a more focus on the low birth rate and long-term care instead of on other issues.

1902
05:06:52,630 --> 05:06:59,529
We would like to clarify here that because this is a budget allocated by various agencies,

1903
05:07:00,090 --> 05:07:09,009
so environmental departments or agricultural departments, they have their budgets allocated for gender issues,

1904
05:07:09,770 --> 05:07:20,209
and for infrastructures that are gender-friendly or for gender-friendly facilities,

1905
05:07:20,709 --> 05:07:25,950
these are also targets of our budgets in various organizations as well.

1906
05:07:25,950 --> 05:07:31,069
I would also like to follow up that from the gender equality department,

1907
05:07:31,529 --> 05:07:47,130
you mentioned how we monitor all of this and supervise as the dedicated organization for the national gender equality organization,

1908
05:07:47,130 --> 05:07:57,470
we ask each ministry or agency to come up to form their own task force for gender equality,

1909
05:07:58,290 --> 05:08:08,909
so it's a complete and comprehensive mechanism, and we have the gender equality policy guidelines that work with our main issues.

1910
05:08:08,909 --> 05:08:18,950
The agencies and ministries, they have their own promotion plans, local governments have their own programs,

1911
05:08:19,610 --> 05:08:33,889
and we have a guidance and review mechanism, and we have a complete set of indicators to monitor and supervise how they perform.

1912
05:08:33,889 --> 05:08:45,790
If they perform under the score of 70, then they become an agency or an organization that requires further guidance,

1913
05:08:45,930 --> 05:08:51,189
and we bring in external experts to help them improve.

1914
05:08:51,610 --> 05:08:58,569
This is how we supervise, and this is something we do once every two years,

1915
05:08:58,569 --> 05:09:05,349
and that performance will be a baseline for our next follow-up to see their improvement,

1916
05:09:05,909 --> 05:09:13,430
and when we look at their performances, they have all improved over the years,

1917
05:09:13,849 --> 05:09:23,630
and for counties or cities that require further assistance or counseling, the numbers are very minimal and lessening.

1918
05:09:24,510 --> 05:09:36,430
Also, every year we ask them to allocate a budget for this year, for the next year, and they allocate a budget for the following four years.

1919
05:09:36,689 --> 05:09:43,450
They set their goals, and the next year we look to see how they have implemented and used the investment.

1920
05:09:43,450 --> 05:09:49,669
If they fail to reach 80 percent or achieve 80 percent of their goals,

1921
05:09:50,150 --> 05:09:58,290
we will also publish all of this information so that everybody knows how the government is spending the budget.

1922
05:09:59,409 --> 05:10:03,209
I'm sorry, the microphone is not on, so the interpreter cannot hear.

1923
05:10:08,149 --> 05:10:13,389
Regarding Article 3, questions for Article 3, anyone would like to follow up?

1924
05:10:13,669 --> 05:10:19,729
No? If not, we would like to thank the comprehensive answering from the Department of Gender Equality.

1925
05:10:19,930 --> 05:10:22,069
We now give the floor back to our reviewers.

1926
05:10:24,630 --> 05:10:34,189
Thank you very much, Honorable Minister, for the comprehensive and detailed responses given.

1927
05:10:34,549 --> 05:10:40,869
However, there were aspects of the question that I'm not sure that I got feedback on.

1928
05:10:41,450 --> 05:10:48,069
I asked about lists and details of those who have received the award, the Crown Award.

1929
05:10:48,069 --> 05:10:52,909
If you have it here, yes, otherwise we would be grateful to receive that,

1930
05:10:53,189 --> 05:11:00,610
as well as the bonuses that you said that some agencies would be giving bonuses,

1931
05:11:01,150 --> 05:11:10,229
how many fall within that category so we can actually have an idea of whether progress is going in the right direction.

1932
05:11:10,229 --> 05:11:21,549
Also, you talked about sectors, sectoral budgets, that it's difficult because the budget that you gave is across sectors,

1933
05:11:21,849 --> 05:11:30,029
and the question is, is it possible for you, if not now, in the future, to disaggregate budget allocation by sector

1934
05:11:30,029 --> 05:11:39,709
so we can actually know in what sector progress towards gender equality is advancing, and that would make it easy for us.

1935
05:11:39,709 --> 05:11:51,009
You talked about the under 70% score, and that becomes like a benchmark, a baseline for discussing going forward,

1936
05:11:51,369 --> 05:11:54,630
so I would just want a little clarification.

1937
05:11:55,209 --> 05:12:01,790
So you have incentives, but there are no sanctions for underperformance.

1938
05:12:01,950 --> 05:12:07,970
Just clarity on that, because what I tend to hear is that you just have an encouragement.

1939
05:12:07,970 --> 05:12:09,310
Is there a sanction?

1940
05:12:10,590 --> 05:12:18,189
Because practices from other jurisdictions might mean that people get a reduction in budgets in the following year

1941
05:12:18,189 --> 05:12:22,189
to the degree that they did not implement a gender budget.

1942
05:12:22,590 --> 05:12:23,669
Is that in place?

1943
05:12:23,930 --> 05:12:35,650
Or what other kind of sanctions to deter people from taking the gender responsive budget as just a paper policy without any bite?

1944
05:12:35,650 --> 05:12:39,049
Thank you. Back to the floor, back to you.

1945
05:12:44,049 --> 05:12:45,169
Thank you.

1946
05:12:48,630 --> 05:12:56,549
So I think some of the data we cannot provide right now, maybe we can come back to you later with information needed,

1947
05:12:56,770 --> 05:13:04,930
and also additional information, whether they are disciplinary actions or what is the benchmark of 70 score,

1948
05:13:04,930 --> 05:13:12,369
maybe we can ask our colleagues to provide oral comments and answers, and we can provide written files.

1949
05:13:12,770 --> 05:13:17,069
So this is Section Chief Shaoding Ting from Department of Gender Equality.

1950
05:13:17,529 --> 05:13:29,090
So for example, the list of the awarded agencies, the details of that and how much bonus that is will be provided later in written details.

1951
05:13:29,090 --> 05:13:39,990
And then for those agencies performing under the benchmark, we would actually disclose their actual final score on the website.

1952
05:13:40,430 --> 05:13:51,509
And then also at the highest level of executive level meeting, that entire score, their performance will be fully disclosed on the meeting.

1953
05:13:51,509 --> 05:14:02,669
And then also the heads of different departments and are very, they actually very care about how their performances are reviewed publicly.

1954
05:14:03,049 --> 05:14:09,290
And then also we also have civil rights, civil society representatives at these meetings.

1955
05:14:09,990 --> 05:14:17,189
And then they would also give advices on how to make improvements so everybody can move forward together.

1956
05:14:18,770 --> 05:14:29,770
Additional information here that when it comes to the actual performance, the score, so last year we had a review meeting,

1957
05:14:29,810 --> 05:14:38,110
so we have the excellence performance over 90 score, and then the A is between 80 to 90 score.

1958
05:14:38,970 --> 05:14:46,069
And then also we have 17 of the departments fail to reach 90 scores, score points.

1959
05:14:46,069 --> 05:14:50,930
And then for the B category, it's between 70 to 80.

1960
05:14:51,389 --> 05:14:55,029
So there are 10 of them in this B category.

1961
05:14:55,130 --> 05:14:59,110
And then we have two that is under 70 points.

1962
05:14:59,389 --> 05:15:04,229
So all this performance, the scorecards are disclosed openly.

1963
05:15:04,630 --> 05:15:10,130
So all the heads of departments are really concerned about their performance going public.

1964
05:15:10,130 --> 05:15:16,630
Therefore, they were really hard to show good scores, even though it's not linked to our budget.

1965
05:15:17,069 --> 05:15:21,810
However, we are doing this with administrative incentive programs.

1966
05:15:22,349 --> 05:15:31,490
And then for the gender budgeting in our report, we do have a breakdown by different departments, and then there are different amounts.

1967
05:15:31,490 --> 05:15:40,389
So because time is limited, we didn't have, didn't cover that, but actually on the websites,

1968
05:15:40,849 --> 05:15:48,470
each one of the divisions and departments would have their gender budgets disclosed openly on the website.

1969
05:15:48,590 --> 05:15:49,869
Thank you for those questions.

1970
05:15:50,689 --> 05:15:54,270
Should we have any written documents and more details?

1971
05:15:54,569 --> 05:16:00,290
We would actually provide them afterward to our IRC members.

1972
05:16:00,290 --> 05:16:02,810
So I'm going to give the floor back to Madame Chair.

1973
05:16:02,889 --> 05:16:04,209
Thank you.

1974
05:16:05,069 --> 05:16:07,430
Thank you very much, delegation.

1975
05:16:08,389 --> 05:16:12,950
Now on Article 4, there are a couple of questions.

1976
05:16:13,470 --> 05:16:21,610
I would like to start by commending the effort that you've made in bringing major gender equality issues to cabinet level

1977
05:16:21,610 --> 05:16:28,689
and facilitating gender equal participation in decision making, both in the public and in the private sector,

1978
05:16:28,689 --> 05:16:40,569
including among national social associations, professional associations, farmers, and the TWSC and TPEC listed companies.

1979
05:16:40,909 --> 05:16:45,630
That's private sector high level companies and the trade unions.

1980
05:16:45,950 --> 05:16:53,630
This is quite encouraging, and I'm sure that progress will be recorded over the years.

1981
05:16:53,630 --> 05:17:01,630
However, on cabinet level representation, there's only nine female cabinet members, which is like 21%.

1982
05:17:03,230 --> 05:17:09,049
Also, managerial level staff who are employed across the country,

1983
05:17:09,770 --> 05:17:14,869
that's moving close to parity over 40%, which is highly commendable.

1984
05:17:15,130 --> 05:17:20,029
But for the cabinet level member, this is below the parity level.

1985
05:17:20,029 --> 05:17:27,490
And so the question is, what efforts are you making to make progress towards parity at the cabinet level?

1986
05:17:28,169 --> 05:17:36,630
With regards to the judiciary, you said number of judges, female to male, are almost at parity.

1987
05:17:37,669 --> 05:17:43,970
So the current gender distribution does not represent under representation.

1988
05:17:43,970 --> 05:17:49,049
However, are there any specialized training from what we've heard?

1989
05:17:49,689 --> 05:17:53,150
The judges themselves are not citing CEDAW sufficiently.

1990
05:17:54,330 --> 05:18:01,349
Application of the Gender Equality Act is not visible in a lot of rulings to the degree that one would expect.

1991
05:18:01,669 --> 05:18:09,409
And so are there any specialized training, accelerated promotion, or other measures to enable the judiciary

1992
05:18:09,409 --> 05:18:15,409
to play its part effectively in implementing commitments under CEDAW?

1993
05:18:15,909 --> 05:18:25,790
With regards to the diplomatic arena, I know that some efforts have been made to increase the number of women in the diplomatic mission.

1994
05:18:26,169 --> 05:18:32,310
But how are you boosting the pipeline? Because the issue you raise is that some of these are based on merit.

1995
05:18:32,310 --> 05:18:43,009
So is there a modality for you to put in place, either through training, equipping, accelerated promotion,

1996
05:18:43,310 --> 05:18:49,409
to have women in the pipeline that can step up into the diplomatic posts?

1997
05:18:51,709 --> 05:18:58,810
You also talk about reforms in terms of appointing people at the executive level,

1998
05:18:58,810 --> 05:19:02,430
using your gender equality policy guidelines.

1999
05:19:03,009 --> 05:19:08,029
What has been the specific outcome of this reform that you've undertaken?

2000
05:19:08,369 --> 05:19:13,709
Are there sectors where you have excelled, and would you be willing to share that with us?

2001
05:19:15,670 --> 05:19:24,349
Before we close this chapter, I would like to really focus on gender and the digital sector, the technology sector.

2002
05:19:24,349 --> 05:19:32,349
I know that you've talked about some incentives for small and medium enterprises and some training, STEM training.

2003
05:19:33,049 --> 05:19:39,810
The question is, how is CEDAW-aligned inclusion being undertaken and ensured by government?

2004
05:19:40,130 --> 05:19:47,049
And what accountability is there to ensure that CEDAW, throughout the technology value chain,

2005
05:19:47,049 --> 05:19:51,509
you've talked just about tech-facilitated gender-based violence.

2006
05:19:51,930 --> 05:19:58,229
You've made progress with that and your sensual imagery center.

2007
05:19:59,250 --> 05:20:05,029
But what about the rest of the value chain and the life cycle of technology itself,

2008
05:20:05,069 --> 05:20:10,770
from ideation to design to deployment and then to application of technology?

2009
05:20:10,770 --> 05:20:20,610
What mechanisms do you have in place to ensure either regulatory mechanisms that are human rights centered or are digitization processes?

2010
05:20:20,849 --> 05:20:22,830
A lot of businesses are going digital.

2011
05:20:23,189 --> 05:20:29,169
Are there guidelines, prototypes to help ensure that they are human rights centered

2012
05:20:29,169 --> 05:20:36,610
and that business models of private sector do not reinvent any form of stereotyping or discrimination?

2013
05:20:36,810 --> 05:20:37,669
Thank you.

2014
05:20:46,470 --> 05:20:47,669
Thank you.

2015
05:20:49,810 --> 05:21:01,909
So for these not very powerful, so the cabinet, well, my colleagues, not issues, the cabinet gender distribution.

2016
05:21:02,849 --> 05:21:06,069
So I would like to ask our colleague to talk about incentives.

2017
05:21:06,169 --> 05:21:07,909
I think it's more a political issue.

2018
05:21:08,049 --> 05:21:09,830
Indeed, it's actually quite challenging.

2019
05:21:09,830 --> 05:21:20,229
And also, we can ask the judicial, yes, the judges, gender issues.

2020
05:21:20,849 --> 05:21:25,310
I think the gender distribution of the judges is not an issue.

2021
05:21:25,490 --> 05:21:29,950
But when it comes to the ruling, are they really reflecting the spirit of CEDAW?

2022
05:21:30,290 --> 05:21:37,610
Are they ongoing on-the-job training to enhance their recognition of gender equality and CEDAW spirits?

2023
05:21:37,610 --> 05:21:47,069
And then also on the diplomatic arena, I would like to ask my colleagues in that domain to answer the question.

2024
05:21:47,110 --> 05:21:51,970
And then do we have any actual outperforming results?

2025
05:21:53,110 --> 05:22:02,470
And then also digitalization, I would like to ask Ministry of Digital Affairs colleagues to talk about that.

2026
05:22:02,470 --> 05:22:15,590
With regard to STEM, so digital-based, gender-based violence, we can ask maybe Ministry of Health and Welfare to answer that.

2027
05:22:15,610 --> 05:22:20,029
And maybe the National Science Council can answer the STEM issue.

2028
05:22:20,310 --> 05:22:28,250
And the SME issue, we can ask the Ministry of Economy to answer that part.

2029
05:22:28,250 --> 05:22:31,389
So maybe we can start with the Cabinet part.

2030
05:22:32,509 --> 05:22:42,450
So this is first time answer the question with regard to Cabinet member, because they are responsible to the enforcement of policies and strategies.

2031
05:22:43,009 --> 05:22:52,849
So Executive Yuan, when it comes to those civil servants promotion, we do not discriminate on the basis of gender, on the ethnicity and races.

2032
05:22:52,849 --> 05:22:58,810
So we would like to retain these talents as long as they are merit-based.

2033
05:22:59,069 --> 05:23:05,529
And then also their talents satisfy the needs of the government policy enforcement.

2034
05:23:06,110 --> 05:23:16,610
The Cabinet's gender distribution indeed is also a very important issue in order to enhance women's political participation in the future.

2035
05:23:16,610 --> 05:23:23,290
So when we retain our talents for Cabinet, we are going to pay more attention to gender equality distribution.

2036
05:23:24,509 --> 05:23:27,590
And for Judicial Yuan, please.

2037
05:23:30,110 --> 05:23:30,930
Thank you.

2038
05:23:31,290 --> 05:23:44,290
For the question, so this is Zhongzhong Lin from Judicial Yuan and from the teens and domestic courts.

2039
05:23:44,290 --> 05:23:53,750
And then now for the CEDAW part, regardless, it's domestic courts or the teens' courts or criminal court courts.

2040
05:23:54,029 --> 05:24:03,889
And then also the actual administrative staff, regardless of their levels, they also need to adopt the CEDAW training courses.

2041
05:24:03,990 --> 05:24:08,909
There are basic entry level and events training courses and workshops.

2042
05:24:08,909 --> 05:24:18,709
So they can really reflect on their ruling, the CEDAW spirits, to events and make sure and safeguard women's rights.

2043
05:24:21,470 --> 05:24:30,669
And then also in our mediation procedures, our mediators, domestic affairs mediators, business and labor disputes mediators,

2044
05:24:30,669 --> 05:24:38,569
they all need to take CEDAW training and specialized education training.

2045
05:24:39,130 --> 05:24:51,349
And then for the actual ruling realization, so on the procedural part, should there be if one party of the litigation is women,

2046
05:24:51,349 --> 05:25:03,630
is there is actual imbalance of power or then the judge would use our court resources or to find other sources,

2047
05:25:03,669 --> 05:25:14,430
resources externally to empower these women and then they can actually help the appointment of attorney and then for domestic disputes.

2048
05:25:14,430 --> 05:25:25,889
And then there are also case handlers to help them and for women and children, especially for the children who cannot really express themselves,

2049
05:25:26,090 --> 05:25:34,409
cannot protect themselves, there would be social workers and also domestic affairs case investigators

2050
05:25:34,409 --> 05:25:43,209
and procedural case handlers to make sure that their human rights are protected during the trial process.

2051
05:25:43,209 --> 05:25:49,349
And whether the education and training can be fully reflected and realized in their ruling.

2052
05:25:49,849 --> 05:25:57,389
In Taiwan, many of the laws and regulations are already amended, so it's up to the judge's discretion,

2053
05:25:57,990 --> 05:26:04,049
especially when it comes to imbalance of power and the woman is on the vulnerable side,

2054
05:26:04,049 --> 05:26:13,569
then the judge have a lot of room for discretion to balance this imbalance of power.

2055
05:26:13,630 --> 05:26:20,849
For example, for domestic affairs, for a vulnerable and a victim of domestic violence for the woman,

2056
05:26:21,790 --> 05:26:31,490
then there will be discretion for the judge so the woman would receive more of the division of alimony

2057
05:26:31,490 --> 05:26:36,889
or the procedural property distribution and then division.

2058
05:26:37,209 --> 05:26:48,650
And then also for DV cases that the vulnerable and the victim who is actually controlled and gaslighted,

2059
05:26:48,770 --> 05:26:58,349
then the perpetrator will take training and then for the vulnerable women, they need to be empowered.

2060
05:26:58,349 --> 05:27:05,970
So there are consultation therapies, counseling services for them so they can be empowered.

2061
05:27:06,130 --> 05:27:11,369
So these are the two main approaches we have.

2062
05:27:11,689 --> 05:27:20,290
But in the ruling that we usually would cite the domestic law without specified CEDAW.

2063
05:27:20,529 --> 05:27:25,250
However, for domestic court ruling and for the teenage court ruling,

2064
05:27:25,250 --> 05:27:28,409
we do have part of the ruling citing CEDAW.

2065
05:27:29,510 --> 05:27:34,229
You can search and see that in our computerized system.

2066
05:27:34,590 --> 05:27:35,209
Okay, MOFA.

2067
05:27:36,970 --> 05:27:41,889
So please raise your hands so our cameraman can find where you are.

2068
05:27:41,930 --> 05:27:47,250
So this is from MOFA, and this is my first time making comments.

2069
05:27:47,409 --> 05:28:00,849
And for the diplomatic female distribution in order to improve the women's participation in diplomatic arena

2070
05:28:00,849 --> 05:28:08,869
and improve gender equality, that for the new incoming training orientation,

2071
05:28:09,729 --> 05:28:16,389
it's on the same ground when we give them training and also we actually see more and more outstanding diplomats.

2072
05:28:16,389 --> 05:28:17,110
They are female.

2073
05:28:17,270 --> 05:28:17,729
They are women.

2074
05:28:18,150 --> 05:28:27,130
Especially you can see the mid-tier management in MOFA that there are more than 50 percent of them are women in recent years.

2075
05:28:28,529 --> 05:28:43,090
And we can see that in our 111 embassies, our main ambassadors take up only about 20 percent.

2076
05:28:43,090 --> 05:28:52,430
But like I said, mid-tier management and higher management altogether is over 37.8 percent.

2077
05:28:52,470 --> 05:29:04,290
I'm sure if we think about the racial of gender and choosing women as management first,

2078
05:29:04,729 --> 05:29:11,229
with this trend, we will have more and more of female directors in these embassies overseas.

2079
05:29:11,229 --> 05:29:15,290
Thank you very much for the answer from MOFA.

2080
05:29:15,790 --> 05:29:23,689
Our Department of Gender Equality will be sharing more about concrete results and excellent performances.

2081
05:29:24,110 --> 05:29:26,450
Thank you very much, reviewers, for your questions.

2082
05:29:27,470 --> 05:29:33,250
You asked about the outstanding performances or excellent performances of our guideline.

2083
05:29:34,250 --> 05:29:44,790
In our policy guideline, we emphasize on narrowing the disparity between decision-making roles.

2084
05:29:45,709 --> 05:29:55,590
And over the years of our promotion plan, there have been many important issues to promote gender equality work.

2085
05:29:55,610 --> 05:30:01,610
And we have a mechanism and we have goals set and we have KPIs set.

2086
05:30:01,610 --> 05:30:04,669
We've made tremendous progress.

2087
05:30:05,770 --> 05:30:18,369
Prior to 2019, we mainly looked at the, for example, we were under the commission of EY.

2088
05:30:18,770 --> 05:30:26,169
And starting from 2005, we have about one-third of the gender ratio.

2089
05:30:26,169 --> 05:30:32,529
And in 2019, we further expanded this gender ratio.

2090
05:30:32,669 --> 05:30:36,069
And there were about 1,700 commissions.

2091
05:30:36,490 --> 05:30:41,590
We gave them two years to improve the gender ratio.

2092
05:30:42,590 --> 05:31:00,409
And in 2022 and 2025, in our action plan, we are striving for a 40% of the seats that are,

2093
05:31:00,569 --> 05:31:04,709
there are no less than 40% of seats of the commissions.

2094
05:31:04,709 --> 05:31:14,709
So of the over 1,700 commissions, there will be a 40% of,

2095
05:31:17,729 --> 05:31:22,270
neither gender should occupy less than 40% of the seats of the committee and missions.

2096
05:31:22,729 --> 05:31:32,770
And if they reach this, they will have, we have now have 98% that has either gender over one-third.

2097
05:31:32,770 --> 05:31:41,349
And 24% growth compared to 2020, which is tremendous growth.

2098
05:31:42,270 --> 05:31:52,509
In 2025, we're going to promote the committees and commissions to have 50-50% of the genders.

2099
05:31:53,310 --> 05:32:04,869
And in terms of the donations of the CSOs that we donate to or we subsidize,

2100
05:32:05,189 --> 05:32:16,209
we want their directors or supervisors and board of directors to have at least one-third of at least women directors and supervisors.

2101
05:32:16,290 --> 05:32:18,590
And there is now 83% of them.

2102
05:32:18,590 --> 05:32:24,830
And also compared to 2020, there is a 17.42% of growth.

2103
05:32:26,330 --> 05:32:40,590
And from 2025 to 2029, we have an action plan that will further promote the gender ratio of 40%

2104
05:32:40,590 --> 05:32:44,869
in all of these board of directors of the CSOs that we subsidize.

2105
05:32:45,869 --> 05:32:58,229
Next, we ask the MODA and MOHW National Science Council and Ministry of Economic Council to take the questions.

2106
05:32:58,849 --> 05:33:10,950
I am from Ministry of Digital Affairs, and in response to women empowerment in the digital era,

2107
05:33:10,950 --> 05:33:21,090
we can see from 2019, we have conducted a five-year survey.

2108
05:33:21,650 --> 05:33:30,430
And through these analysis, we now understand about the women disparity.

2109
05:33:30,909 --> 05:33:39,130
Women over 12 years old, there is a 4.3% gap in their digital capability.

2110
05:33:39,130 --> 05:33:47,290
But if we factor in disability and ages above 70 years old, and we look at the survey of accessibility,

2111
05:33:47,470 --> 05:33:53,290
there is a greater ratio, including women with disabilities.

2112
05:33:54,009 --> 05:34:01,169
They have less than 11% compared to men.

2113
05:34:01,169 --> 05:34:12,869
And women ages 70 to 74 is about 15.6% behind the same male ages.

2114
05:34:13,409 --> 05:34:21,790
And if we look at all of this, we look at these surveys and we respond these surveys back to the ministries

2115
05:34:21,790 --> 05:34:30,150
to see how they can prioritize their accessibility to elderly and people with disabilities or new immigrants.

2116
05:34:30,150 --> 05:34:34,490
And to enable them to participate in digital empowerment.

2117
05:34:35,069 --> 05:34:43,610
And we start with women-friendly empowerment and we look at incapacity building.

2118
05:34:43,930 --> 05:34:52,349
For example, we're lowering barriers in terms of their time, location, and responsibility of care and duty of care.

2119
05:34:52,349 --> 05:34:58,049
So the timings and the venues of the trainings are friendly for women.

2120
05:34:59,169 --> 05:35:05,009
And we look at and to further enhance their identification.

2121
05:35:05,430 --> 05:35:15,189
And we hold these trainings during the weekdays or holidays or online so that female has more accessibility to these trainings.

2122
05:35:15,189 --> 05:35:22,990
We invite female speakers, invite female entrepreneurs to speak to them.

2123
05:35:23,169 --> 05:35:33,990
For example, last year we held over 30 capacity building sessions, over half are for women.

2124
05:35:34,270 --> 05:35:41,590
If we focus on AI and information security, we hosted 17 sessions.

2125
05:35:41,590 --> 05:35:48,669
And there were over 1,000 women who participated, which is more than 36%.

2126
05:35:49,590 --> 05:35:50,090
Thank you.

2127
05:35:50,150 --> 05:35:58,729
The Ministry of Health and Welfare, I am the Director General of Protective Agency.

2128
05:35:59,470 --> 05:36:10,790
When we talk about the digital gender-based violence facilitated by technology, it's something we require cross-department cooperation.

2129
05:36:10,790 --> 05:36:22,970
So in addition to amending our Juvenile Sexual Exploitation Act in 2019,

2130
05:36:23,590 --> 05:36:35,409
we further included the juvenile images, sexual images in the scope of sexual exploitation in 2023 under the guidance of EY,

2131
05:36:35,409 --> 05:36:40,689
including Minister of Health and Welfare, judicial departments and relevant departments.

2132
05:36:40,990 --> 05:36:50,090
We started amending the four laws of the sexual harassment and violence.

2133
05:36:50,630 --> 05:36:58,150
And in recent years, we have further managed and revised acts as appropriate.

2134
05:36:58,750 --> 05:37:00,430
These are ongoing progress.

2135
05:37:00,430 --> 05:37:07,990
That is our determination to strengthen the duty of protection of this government.

2136
05:37:08,529 --> 05:37:25,450
And we established a single-wind mailbox that is a one-stop mailbox that operates 24-7, 365 days to receive complaints regarding sexual images,

2137
05:37:26,529 --> 05:37:31,189
to immediately remove the sexual images as appropriate.

2138
05:37:31,270 --> 05:37:41,610
And in addition to using technology, we use technology to proactively stop all of these sexual images instead of just waiting for the complaints.

2139
05:37:41,750 --> 05:37:47,029
And we also use AI technology to improve our administrative efficiency.

2140
05:37:47,029 --> 05:37:53,330
We also work with the NGOs and local governments to provide service to our victims.

2141
05:37:56,930 --> 05:37:59,729
We now give the floor to National Science Council.

2142
05:38:03,970 --> 05:38:11,430
Regarding the investment in STEM, the Ministry of Education already has budgets and programs.

2143
05:38:12,430 --> 05:38:30,209
And to improve the gender segregation in technology domain in 2022, we hosted seminars for females in STEM.

2144
05:38:30,590 --> 05:38:37,849
And we also invite them to come and share their experiences and to talk about their career development

2145
05:38:37,849 --> 05:38:48,290
and to build a friendly environment for research and also to encourage more female engineers to join us.

2146
05:38:49,689 --> 05:39:02,330
We also have more and more female-leading and chairing National Science Council programs from 26.2 percent in 2020 to 27.5 percent in 2024.

2147
05:39:02,330 --> 05:39:07,909
Does the Ministry of Education would like to follow up on STEM?

2148
05:39:09,770 --> 05:39:12,790
Because National Science Council mentioned Ministry of Education.

2149
05:39:13,349 --> 05:39:19,049
Yes, this is from the Higher Education Office at Ministry of Education.

2150
05:39:20,569 --> 05:39:26,349
Regarding college students majoring in STEM domain,

2151
05:39:26,349 --> 05:39:39,830
we basically have programs to create gender-friendly learning environment on campus and to provide fundings to subsidize.

2152
05:39:39,830 --> 05:39:49,389
In 2024, we have over 90,000 students taking up STEM as a major,

2153
05:39:49,950 --> 05:40:04,369
among which female students account for 43,000, which is about 46.9 percent, and the number is growing over the years.

2154
05:40:04,369 --> 05:40:15,630
And in addition to college students and female students, regarding female teachers and researchers at our ministry,

2155
05:40:16,250 --> 05:40:29,990
we have a program to empower and encourage female science and STEM research talents, and we provide subsidies.

2156
05:40:30,770 --> 05:40:32,529
That's our follow-up to the answer.

2157
05:40:32,529 --> 05:40:33,630
Thank you very much.

2158
05:40:34,069 --> 05:40:40,950
Finally, we give the floor to the Ministry of Economic Affairs about gender equality in SMEs.

2159
05:40:42,569 --> 05:40:47,970
I am the Deputy Director at Sexual Development.

2160
05:40:48,669 --> 05:41:01,270
And in order to encourage female to participate economically in STEM or technology industries,

2161
05:41:01,270 --> 05:41:07,470
we have relevant talent trainings, and we guarantee female quota.

2162
05:41:07,810 --> 05:41:21,029
For example, for semiconductor talent training, we reserve 20 percent availability for the female.

2163
05:41:21,029 --> 05:41:38,029
And we also hosted seminars and training courses for corporates and corporate managements to talk about gender mainstreaming.

2164
05:41:38,229 --> 05:41:51,630
And we also have, if science or tech companies, manufacturing companies, they are applying for awards or subsidies at our ministries,

2165
05:41:51,630 --> 05:42:00,770
we ask that they submit applications that include programs to create a gender-friendly workplace,

2166
05:42:02,529 --> 05:42:15,290
including hiring a new hire female researchers as one of the criteria that we evaluate their programs on.

2167
05:42:15,290 --> 05:42:18,409
That's how we guarantee female employment.

2168
05:42:18,569 --> 05:42:19,470
Thank you very much.

2169
05:42:19,470 --> 05:42:26,330
We have these various ministries that answered the questions provided by the reviewers.

2170
05:42:26,470 --> 05:42:33,349
I would like to ask, are there any other ministries that would like to follow up before we give the floor back to the reviewers?

2171
05:42:33,610 --> 05:42:40,669
If there are no follow-ups, we would like to thank all of you for your answering, and now we give the floor back to our reviewers.

2172
05:42:41,009 --> 05:42:41,869
Thank you.

2173
05:42:42,729 --> 05:42:49,209
Thank you very much, the head of the delegation, for the extensive answers across sectors.

2174
05:42:50,189 --> 05:42:59,349
Obviously, a lot of work is ongoing, and we hope that some of those results will begin to be evident in the years ahead.

2175
05:43:00,310 --> 05:43:05,049
Some of them might need sharpening, and I know that my colleague has some questions,

2176
05:43:05,049 --> 05:43:08,430
but I would like to respond to the Ministry of Justice.

2177
05:43:08,849 --> 05:43:17,869
Just to ask, because you talked about training and the use of judges' discretion in the application of CEDAW,

2178
05:43:18,150 --> 05:43:24,009
and to share the experience from my own home country where I have been involved in working with the judiciary

2179
05:43:25,010 --> 05:43:31,090
in developing judicial protocols, guidelines, bench books,

2180
05:43:31,290 --> 05:43:37,990
to guide the judiciary at different tiers of government, the Magistrate Court, the Sharia Court,

2181
05:43:38,369 --> 05:43:44,090
in terms of how they can better deliver on the application of CEDAW in their day-to-day.

2182
05:43:44,270 --> 05:43:50,470
And some of those tools are things that you might want to consider, because you already have the law.

2183
05:43:50,470 --> 05:43:59,169
Just like in my country, the laws are in place, the constitution is supportive, but the application is constrained.

2184
05:43:59,470 --> 05:44:05,810
And so the work has been to develop bench books, checklists, judicial protocol,

2185
05:44:06,229 --> 05:44:12,650
as well as case management guide at every level of the judicial system to help them to deliver.

2186
05:44:12,709 --> 05:44:17,849
So I just thought to share that with you, that it's some kind of recommendation you might want to consider

2187
05:44:17,849 --> 05:44:25,529
that would help the judiciary to better deliver on the very, very noble aspirations of government and the law that you have.

2188
05:44:25,830 --> 05:44:30,790
And I'll yield the floor now to Marion, who has maybe a few questions before we move to Article 5.

2189
05:44:30,790 --> 05:44:33,529
Oh, and you too, Heisu? Okay. Marion?

2190
05:44:35,590 --> 05:44:37,130
Thank you very much, Madam Chair.

2191
05:44:37,450 --> 05:44:44,290
I'd just like to ask the Taiwan delegation about the use of TSM's temporary special measures

2192
05:44:44,290 --> 05:44:53,250
in the renewable energy sector, given that we have increasing challenges in terms of climate crisis.

2193
05:44:54,310 --> 05:44:58,869
Typhoon Bavi went north of Taiwan, I think, and so that was very fortunate.

2194
05:44:59,330 --> 05:45:07,290
But my question really is around the mandate that Taiwan has in terms of green growth net zero emissions by 2050.

2195
05:45:07,729 --> 05:45:13,610
And there is a national development plan that is in place, spearheaded by the National Development Council,

2196
05:45:13,610 --> 05:45:20,930
that is really looking at this mandate and trying to reach this particular goal.

2197
05:45:21,270 --> 05:45:27,409
And so my question is, do women, including rural women and indigenous women in Taiwan,

2198
05:45:27,889 --> 05:45:35,270
have a significant and meaningful role in advancing the initiative of green growth net zero emissions?

2199
05:45:35,270 --> 05:45:42,990
This has implications for not only for their social and economic empowerment, but their leadership and decision making.

2200
05:45:43,610 --> 05:45:50,270
And so has the State Party considered using temporary special measures to increase the capacity

2201
05:45:50,270 --> 05:45:55,470
and the active participation of women in this renewable energy sector?

2202
05:45:59,490 --> 05:46:00,330
Thank you. Heisu?

2203
05:46:00,330 --> 05:46:04,409
Thank you. A very short question to the Judicial Yuan.

2204
05:46:05,349 --> 05:46:13,189
You said that there is training on CEDAW, the convention provided to the judges.

2205
05:46:13,849 --> 05:46:20,610
And who are the trainers who provide training on CEDAW?

2206
05:46:21,389 --> 05:46:23,090
So that would be my question.

2207
05:46:23,090 --> 05:46:29,229
But Madam Chair, if you allow me, I just want to ask a follow-up question,

2208
05:46:29,290 --> 05:46:34,130
one follow-up question regarding the implementation of CEDAW by the Department of Gender Equality.

2209
05:46:35,750 --> 05:46:46,810
And thanks for all the explanation regarding evaluation of implementation across department system

2210
05:46:46,810 --> 05:46:51,729
that you put on website, how they are graded in terms of implementation.

2211
05:46:51,729 --> 05:47:00,090
My question is, how do you monitor implementation of CEDAW convention by the local government?

2212
05:47:00,669 --> 05:47:03,709
I think it's all done at the central government level.

2213
05:47:04,849 --> 05:47:18,110
So there is a concern raised that the CEDAW convention in Taiwan is difficult to reach to the remote areas at the local government level,

2214
05:47:18,110 --> 05:47:30,669
to the different cities in different, like Kaohsiung or other cities that do not domesticate the convention yet.

2215
05:47:30,990 --> 05:47:35,069
So that would be my additional question. Thank you.

2216
05:47:36,330 --> 05:47:42,450
So for the delegation, if we have a quick response, we can go to Article 5. Thank you.

2217
05:47:47,430 --> 05:47:55,090
Thank you. Thank you, Madam Chair, for offering us your tool.

2218
05:47:55,250 --> 05:47:58,069
I think that's going to be very valuable.

2219
05:47:58,409 --> 05:48:05,130
So to answer the three questions, I would like to now give the floor to our colleagues for renewable energy.

2220
05:48:05,250 --> 05:48:09,270
I would like to ask the Ministry of Economic Affairs to answer that.

2221
05:48:09,270 --> 05:48:13,189
And the Council of Indigenous Affairs can also answer that.

2222
05:48:13,389 --> 05:48:20,150
And then when it comes to the local issue, should there be indigenous areas involved?

2223
05:48:20,330 --> 05:48:31,229
Maybe our CIP, Council of Indigenous Affairs, can also provide additional information to actually see how CEDAW is implemented locally.

2224
05:48:31,229 --> 05:48:34,009
And then that's about renewable energy.

2225
05:48:35,150 --> 05:48:45,229
And if our Ministry of Environment can also offer additional information after CIP and after Ministry of Economic Affairs.

2226
05:48:45,569 --> 05:48:53,049
And then I would like to ask the Judicial Yuan to answer about who are the trainers of CEDAW.

2227
05:48:53,349 --> 05:48:59,549
And then we would ask the CIP to offer the additional information.

2228
05:48:59,549 --> 05:49:03,630
And we have so many different departments, so please be cautious of time.

2229
05:49:03,689 --> 05:49:04,549
Thank you.

2230
05:49:07,290 --> 05:49:08,689
MOEA, you can go first.

2231
05:49:09,709 --> 05:49:10,009
Yes.

2232
05:49:10,750 --> 05:49:17,090
So about the industry development department, this is the deputy director general.

2233
05:49:18,549 --> 05:49:24,669
So for renewable energy and net zero emission, that is a world trend.

2234
05:49:24,669 --> 05:49:29,990
And then indeed, it is also a pillar policy here in Taiwan.

2235
05:49:30,369 --> 05:49:42,009
And if we really want to hit our net zero goal, then there are many of the inventory work of carbon footprint calculation we need to do.

2236
05:49:42,229 --> 05:49:46,790
And then we need to have experts and specialists in that area.

2237
05:49:46,790 --> 05:50:00,310
And so like the STEM, for the training, we would definitely have secured slots reserved for women so they can take part in the training.

2238
05:50:00,430 --> 05:50:07,490
And then later, we would actually match them with those business in needs to provide these kind of work.

2239
05:50:07,490 --> 05:50:16,770
And also, we would coach business for net zero and for renewable energy adoption.

2240
05:50:17,290 --> 05:50:25,310
And when they come to MOEA to make their proposal, they need to answer to their gender equality requirements.

2241
05:50:25,310 --> 05:50:37,669
Are they give more reserved or affirmative ratio to women, or are they offering parental leave benefits?

2242
05:50:37,909 --> 05:50:49,310
They have to make very clear proposals in that, so that will be factor into our programs.

2243
05:50:49,310 --> 05:50:56,169
So any other additional information on renewable energy from CIP?

2244
05:50:56,209 --> 05:50:57,409
This is from CIP.

2245
05:50:58,349 --> 05:51:10,729
So with regards for indigenous business and industry development, from 2015, we started to give them coach programs for entrepreneurs.

2246
05:51:11,430 --> 05:51:16,430
So the indigenous entrepreneurs will receive training and coaching as seed fund.

2247
05:51:16,430 --> 05:51:29,130
And then also, our coach would actually support and coach them for six months to enhance the team's competitiveness.

2248
05:51:29,689 --> 05:51:42,349
So as of 2020, between 2021 to 2024, we have supported altogether 39 indigenous businesswomen who successfully started their own career and business.

2249
05:51:42,349 --> 05:51:46,470
Any other information on renewable energy?

2250
05:51:50,830 --> 05:51:52,869
If not, you can say no.

2251
05:52:01,029 --> 05:52:05,490
So Ministry of Environment, first time making comments.

2252
05:52:05,869 --> 05:52:09,349
So we don't have additional information with regard to renewable energy.

2253
05:52:09,349 --> 05:52:09,869
Okay.

2254
05:52:10,409 --> 05:52:15,090
Thank you for your question.

2255
05:52:19,830 --> 05:52:26,909
So this is the teenage cult's head.

2256
05:52:27,229 --> 05:52:39,090
So all these ruling judges of Taiwan, you all have to receive gender equity education, which is designed on the basis of pseudo-spirits.

2257
05:52:39,090 --> 05:52:42,430
So there are four kinds of trainings.

2258
05:52:43,209 --> 05:52:44,250
So who are the coaches?

2259
05:52:44,709 --> 05:52:56,450
They are instructors and trainers from famous gender institutes across universities in Taiwan.

2260
05:52:56,529 --> 05:53:05,090
So these are our trainer and also the professional and professors offering counseling and therapy services.

2261
05:53:05,509 --> 05:53:08,729
They would have a team to give training.

2262
05:53:09,150 --> 05:53:13,009
And then also, we would invite overseas experts.

2263
05:53:13,450 --> 05:53:19,950
Sometimes they would deliver the training online or sometimes they will come here in person.

2264
05:53:19,950 --> 05:53:38,290
And the last type, that for senior judges in Taiwan, they have accumulated a lot of experiences in empowering women and gender equality in their court practice.

2265
05:53:38,430 --> 05:53:44,130
And then we would actually invite them over to share real world cases and their practices.

2266
05:53:44,130 --> 05:53:50,770
So we would like to ask Department of Gender Equality to answer the local implementation.

2267
05:53:51,349 --> 05:53:59,970
So in terms of the local implementation of CEDAW, so at central level and local, we have this local government autonomy.

2268
05:54:01,569 --> 05:54:06,310
So for the CEDAW, so we started with central government.

2269
05:54:06,310 --> 05:54:14,549
And then because the local government, they are critical because they are the first line to have engagement with our citizens.

2270
05:54:14,869 --> 05:54:17,549
So they are required to have CEDAW training.

2271
05:54:17,669 --> 05:54:23,729
And then also for our evaluation indicators, how did they implement CEDAW?

2272
05:54:23,790 --> 05:54:28,189
So they do have education training requirement and the measures.

2273
05:54:28,189 --> 05:54:40,209
And then also our observation conclusions can also, for them, serve as a reference for them.

2274
05:54:40,250 --> 05:54:44,729
And also in the latest program, we would like to ask them to offer a CEDAW city report.

2275
05:54:44,750 --> 05:54:53,229
So we have new Taipei city, Taoyuan, and Taichung cities are now starting to work on city and municipal level reports.

2276
05:54:53,349 --> 05:54:57,490
So this is actually direction we hope they will be driving toward to.

2277
05:54:57,490 --> 05:54:58,450
Thank you.

2278
05:54:59,209 --> 05:55:06,430
So CIP, anything about additional information to offer with regard to indigenous affairs?

2279
05:55:08,090 --> 05:55:09,430
So additional information.

2280
05:55:10,470 --> 05:55:21,869
So indigenous regions for its CEDAW implementation so far that we do have a gender equality task force.

2281
05:55:21,869 --> 05:55:28,069
So we actually focus on their women's participation in the local councils.

2282
05:55:28,430 --> 05:55:37,529
And because in the indigenous areas for development, that they need to get consent from the local indigenous council.

2283
05:55:38,009 --> 05:55:51,209
So at the moment, in terms of the women's participation, that we are reminded by scholars and experts that the female representation in these indigenous councils are quite low.

2284
05:55:51,209 --> 05:55:59,709
Therefore, we are working together with this township offices in these indigenous areas.

2285
05:55:59,810 --> 05:56:04,689
We would like to know the reasons of these low female presentation in indigenous councils.

2286
05:56:04,869 --> 05:56:15,470
And going forward, we are going to work together with the township offices to encourage women's participation in indigenous council and their involvement in decision making.

2287
05:56:15,669 --> 05:56:19,009
So this is ongoing progress right now.

2288
05:56:19,770 --> 05:56:28,010
Thank you very much for all the additional information anyone would like to add on.

2289
05:56:30,909 --> 05:56:33,709
If none, thank you very much.

2290
05:56:33,750 --> 05:56:38,150
Now I'm going to give the floor back to our review committee.

2291
05:56:49,009 --> 05:56:49,750
Thank you.

2292
05:56:51,009 --> 05:56:53,169
Now going to Article 5.

2293
05:56:53,770 --> 05:56:56,009
Professor Leti, are you the one taking over?

2294
05:56:59,389 --> 05:57:00,549
Thank you, Madam Chair.

2295
05:57:01,650 --> 05:57:06,630
Article 5 addresses gender stereotypes and gender-based violence against women.

2296
05:57:07,150 --> 05:57:09,290
So in regard to gender stereotypes,

2297
05:57:12,309 --> 05:57:18,290
the committee also welcomes the numerous initiatives undertaken to challenge gender stereotypes,

2298
05:57:19,729 --> 05:57:32,209
including public awareness campaigns, educational reforms, cultural initiatives, and efforts to reduce occupational segregation and promote women's participation in traditionally male-dominated sectors.

2299
05:57:32,209 --> 05:57:39,529
However, despite these positive developments, gender stereotypes remain deeply embedded in social attitudes and institutions.

2300
05:57:40,310 --> 05:57:47,830
The committee notes continuing reports of victim blaming narratives, particularly in media coverage of gender-based violence,

2301
05:57:48,229 --> 05:58:01,250
and remains concerned that many of the measures adopted appear to focus primarily on awareness raising rather than addressing the underlying patriarchal norms that perpetuate discrimination and violence.

2302
05:58:01,250 --> 05:58:13,250
So can the delegation elaborate on whether the State Party intends to adopt a comprehensive strategy and program to eliminate discriminatory gender stereotypes, both online and offline?

2303
05:58:14,209 --> 05:58:24,490
In particular, what measures are being taken to ensure systematic training of public officials and media professionals to promote gender-responsive media reporting

2304
05:58:24,490 --> 05:58:36,490
and to address stereotypes affecting women in marginalized situations, including Indigenous women, migrant women, women with disabilities, older women, and LBTI women?

2305
05:58:37,389 --> 05:58:39,369
I now turn to gender-based violence.

2306
05:58:40,009 --> 05:58:48,250
The committee welcomes the considerable efforts undertaken by the State Party since the previous review to strengthen its legislative and policy framework.

2307
05:58:48,250 --> 05:58:58,290
We note in particular the adoption of the National Action Plan for Gender-Based Violence Prevention of 2025, the amendments to the Domestic Violence Prevention Act,

2308
05:58:58,650 --> 05:59:05,450
the Sexual Harassment Prevention Act, the Gender Equality and Employment Act, the Gender Equity Education Act,

2309
05:59:05,729 --> 05:59:12,950
as well as reforms to legislation addressing sexual assault, stalking, and technology-facilitated gender-based violence.

2310
05:59:12,950 --> 05:59:21,650
These developments demonstrate the State Party's continued commitment to preventing violence against women and strengthening victim protection.

2311
05:59:22,290 --> 05:59:33,549
Nevertheless, as the committee emphasized in its General Recommendation No. 35, legislation alone is insufficient unless accompanied by coordinated implementation,

2312
05:59:34,270 --> 05:59:39,909
adequate resources, and measures addressing the structural causes of gender-based violence.

2313
05:59:39,909 --> 05:59:50,229
So the committee welcomes the establishment of the National Action Plan for Gender-Based Violence, which has the potential to provide a more integrated response to violence against women.

2314
05:59:51,490 --> 06:00:05,689
So can you please elaborate on how the National Action Plan addresses the structural causes of gender-based violence, ensures coordination across sectors, and establishes clear accountability and monitoring mechanisms?

2315
06:00:05,689 --> 06:00:20,310
Furthermore, how does the State Party ensure that all forms of gender-based violence against women are addressed as manifestations of gender inequality and discrimination, consistent with GR No. 35?

2316
06:00:21,310 --> 06:00:29,750
In regard to domestic violence, the committee welcomes the amendments made to the Domestic Violence Prevention Act, the strengthening of protection orders,

2317
06:00:29,750 --> 06:00:36,009
the establishment of cross-sector safety networks, and the expansion of services available to victims.

2318
06:00:36,450 --> 06:00:42,750
These represent important advances in protection of women experiencing domestic violence.

2319
06:00:43,270 --> 06:00:52,150
Nevertheless, the statistics provided by the State Party indicate that the number of reported domestic violence victims has continued to increase,

2320
06:00:52,610 --> 06:00:57,110
while women consistently account for approximately three quarters of all victims.

2321
06:00:57,110 --> 06:01:03,889
The committee also notes the continued prevalence of intimate partner violence, particularly among certain groups of women.

2322
06:01:04,569 --> 06:01:12,830
Can the delegation explain how it interprets these trends and what additional measures are envisaged to reduce the prevalence of domestic violence?

2323
06:01:13,250 --> 06:01:22,349
In particular, how does the State Party ensure that the amendments to the Domestic Violence Prevention Act are effectively translated into practice,

2324
06:01:22,349 --> 06:01:27,889
including through adequate resources, coordinated implementation, and effective monitoring?

2325
06:01:28,630 --> 06:01:34,830
The committee also notes concerns regarding inconsistencies in perpetrator intervention programs,

2326
06:01:35,450 --> 06:01:44,310
regional disparities in victim services, and continuing challenges in ensuring effective protection following the issuance of protection orders.

2327
06:01:44,310 --> 06:01:52,770
The question is, what measures are being taken to strengthen perpetrator programs, improve coordination between relevant authorities,

2328
06:01:53,330 --> 06:02:02,970
and ensure that protection orders provide timely and effective protection to victims in accordance with the State Party's due diligence obligations under the Convention?

2329
06:02:04,069 --> 06:02:05,950
I now move to sexual harassment.

2330
06:02:05,950 --> 06:02:13,549
The committee welcomes the comprehensive amendments adopted in 2023 to the Gender Equality and Employment Act,

2331
06:02:13,729 --> 06:02:21,069
the Sexual Harassment Prevention Act, and the Gender Equity Education Act, which strengthens victim protection,

2332
06:02:21,610 --> 06:02:26,229
improves complaint mechanisms, and increases accountability for perpetrators.

2333
06:02:26,229 --> 06:02:36,610
Can the delegation share the factors underlying the increases in sexual harassment and indicate whether they reflect improved reporting,

2334
06:02:37,630 --> 06:02:40,529
increased prevalence, or remaining gaps in prevention?

2335
06:02:41,470 --> 06:02:47,569
Furthermore, what measures are being taken to ensure the effective implementation of the three acts,

2336
06:02:47,569 --> 06:02:56,990
including trauma-informed procedures, effective investigation of complaints, protection against retaliation, and adequate remedies for victims?

2337
06:02:58,250 --> 06:03:06,409
In regard to sexual assault, the committee welcomes the increased funding allocated through the Domestic Violence and Sexual Assault Prevention Fund,

2338
06:03:06,930 --> 06:03:14,669
the strengthening of professional training for judicial and social work personnel, and the measures introduced to improve victim protection.

2339
06:03:14,669 --> 06:03:22,770
At the same time, the committee notes that women continue to account for more than 80% of reported victims of sexual assault

2340
06:03:22,770 --> 06:03:30,770
and that certain groups, including immigrant women, indigenous women, and women with disabilities, remain disproportionately affected.

2341
06:03:31,389 --> 06:03:39,750
Could the delegation explain how it addresses these disparities and whether the State Party explicitly recognizes sexual assault

2342
06:03:39,750 --> 06:03:46,330
as a form of gender-based violence rooted in structural discrimination and unequal power relations?

2343
06:03:47,290 --> 06:03:52,709
The committee also notes the information provided regarding convictions in sexual assault cases.

2344
06:03:53,130 --> 06:04:02,669
However, concerns remain regarding the attrition of cases within the justice system and the barriers faced by survivors in obtaining effective remedies.

2345
06:04:02,669 --> 06:04:10,670
My final question is, can the delegation explain what measures are being taken to strengthen access to justice for survivors,

2346
06:04:11,830 --> 06:04:22,670
including through trauma-informed investigations and judicial proceedings, systematic monitoring of prosecution outcomes, and measures to combat victim-blaming attitudes?

2347
06:04:22,930 --> 06:04:33,430
In this regard, how does the State Party ensure compliance with the principles set out in General Recommendation No. 33 on women's access to justice

2348
06:04:33,430 --> 06:04:38,189
and General Recommendation No. 35 on gender-based violence against women?

2349
06:04:38,869 --> 06:04:40,029
Thank you, Madam Chair.

2350
06:04:42,810 --> 06:04:47,849
Thank you. Now we give the floor to the delegation for responses to these questions. Thank you.

2351
06:05:01,510 --> 06:05:04,790
Thank you very much.

2352
06:05:08,450 --> 06:05:20,970
Regarding the Harassment Prevention Act, we would like to ask the Ministry of Labor and Ministry of Health,

2353
06:05:21,970 --> 06:05:28,450
Ministry of Education, Ministry of Interior, Stalking and Harassment is Ministry of Interior,

2354
06:05:29,970 --> 06:05:44,569
and for GBV Prevention Act is going to be taken by the Judicial Yuan and the Ministry of Health and Welfare.

2355
06:05:48,409 --> 06:06:01,950
Judicial Yuan, you're going to talk about the judicial proceeding regarding the sexual assault and for unequal rights relation.

2356
06:06:02,549 --> 06:06:12,130
We talk about survival obstacles, barriers faced by the survivors, and also trauma-informed consultation.

2357
06:06:13,310 --> 06:06:24,930
We asked the Minister of Health and Welfare to talk about the three Gender Equality Acts.

2358
06:06:25,830 --> 06:06:33,549
There were a number of questions. Can I comprehensively answer what I have noted down?

2359
06:06:33,549 --> 06:06:38,909
First of all, we talked about gender-based violence.

2360
06:06:39,229 --> 06:06:45,830
We believe that post-violence service is very important, but prevention is more important,

2361
06:06:45,889 --> 06:06:51,290
and that answers and echoes our preventive strategies.

2362
06:06:51,669 --> 06:06:59,770
When we started with very limited resources, we responded after the events and the incidents.

2363
06:06:59,770 --> 06:07:08,209
So we start from strengthening the protection of victims to allocate our resources,

2364
06:07:08,450 --> 06:07:17,630
but we also realize that only when we intervene early will we be able to help the victims recover better.

2365
06:07:18,110 --> 06:07:25,970
And what's different about Taiwan is in terms of GBV prevention and gender-based violence,

2366
06:07:28,530 --> 06:07:33,509
it's a complaint-based system.

2367
06:07:34,549 --> 06:07:47,849
When we talk about we have to, oh sorry, in Taiwan it's not a complaint-based, it's we report when we see it.

2368
06:07:48,229 --> 06:07:52,669
So the numbers that you see that are increasing, we don't see it as a bad thing

2369
06:07:52,669 --> 06:07:58,270
because we're also doing a prevalence survey over the past eight years.

2370
06:07:58,650 --> 06:08:05,509
There's been two surveys, and we're moving into a third national prevalence survey,

2371
06:08:05,709 --> 06:08:14,430
and we've noticed that female victims of domestic violence and the prevalence rate of it

2372
06:08:14,430 --> 06:08:24,650
is the first time we see 25% of women who face intimate relationship violence throughout their lives.

2373
06:08:24,709 --> 06:08:29,430
That was in the first survey, but in the second survey the number lowered to 20%.

2374
06:08:29,430 --> 06:08:34,049
During this time our number of reports still increased,

2375
06:08:34,310 --> 06:08:40,110
which means we are seeing more and more of the hidden numbers that are being revealed now.

2376
06:08:40,110 --> 06:08:51,310
And even though we see an increase in the numbers reported, in 2024 we further amended our acts.

2377
06:08:51,650 --> 06:08:57,569
In the past the victims would have to file the complaints and reappeal,

2378
06:08:57,610 --> 06:09:04,110
but now they only have to file the complaint once and we will start the investigation.

2379
06:09:04,389 --> 06:09:13,750
And also we keep the date, all of their information confidential.

2380
06:09:15,409 --> 06:09:23,529
And as our viewers have mentioned, you wondered how victims, why are the majority of the victims,

2381
06:09:23,610 --> 06:09:30,889
and you see a larger number in foreign women and indigenous women.

2382
06:09:30,889 --> 06:09:36,930
The absolute majority is still Taiwanese citizens,

2383
06:09:37,529 --> 06:09:46,069
but what you're seeing is the rate of the violence they suffered

2384
06:09:46,069 --> 06:09:56,330
because they have a smaller number to start with, so with a smaller base number the ratio would be higher.

2385
06:09:57,330 --> 06:10:04,049
And it also has to do with the level of information they have access to,

2386
06:10:04,209 --> 06:10:06,990
and also their willingness to seek help.

2387
06:10:07,229 --> 06:10:15,849
And we work hard to remove the barriers to their accessibility.

2388
06:10:18,029 --> 06:10:20,790
Next we give the floor to Ministry of Labor.

2389
06:10:24,590 --> 06:10:26,930
And good afternoon everyone.

2390
06:10:27,909 --> 06:10:35,770
Thank you very much for caring about our Gender Equality in Employment Act

2391
06:10:35,770 --> 06:10:47,069
and how we have performed after the amendment since its enforcement in March 8, 2024

2392
06:10:47,069 --> 06:10:53,889
for the Employment Harassment, Sexual Harassment Act.

2393
06:10:54,610 --> 06:11:01,209
The main difference is in the past if the employer does not handle it,

2394
06:11:01,509 --> 06:11:08,709
or if the victim is not satisfied with the treatment,

2395
06:11:08,709 --> 06:11:14,709
they can appeal to the local competent authority.

2396
06:11:15,509 --> 06:11:24,709
So we can see in practice there are some cases where victims are not happy

2397
06:11:25,509 --> 06:11:34,830
with how the case has been processed, and they appeal to the competent authority.

2398
06:11:35,830 --> 06:11:39,630
So the competent authority can start an investigation

2399
06:11:39,630 --> 06:11:46,389
and require and mandate the employer for further treatment.

2400
06:11:47,290 --> 06:12:00,709
In the past the person responsible in the enterprise can now appeal to the competent authority

2401
06:12:00,709 --> 06:12:06,529
so that the victim no longer need to go through the internal investigations.

2402
06:12:07,409 --> 06:12:13,250
So this protection is more comprehensive for the victim.

2403
06:12:13,490 --> 06:12:17,189
And also we talk about retaliation and revenge.

2404
06:12:18,689 --> 06:12:31,689
Our Act itself states that the labor may not face disadvantaged treatment

2405
06:12:31,689 --> 06:12:33,869
because of the appeal or complaint.

2406
06:12:34,430 --> 06:12:42,569
But we also ask the employer in our amendment to implement monitoring

2407
06:12:42,569 --> 06:12:47,029
and performance and follow-up to prevent retaliation and revenge.

2408
06:12:47,490 --> 06:12:54,770
So we have these in package in conjunction with all of these current amendments.

2409
06:12:55,049 --> 06:12:55,630
Thank you.

2410
06:12:56,130 --> 06:12:58,810
Before we give the floor to Ministry of Education,

2411
06:12:58,849 --> 06:13:08,569
I would like to follow up because the reviewers asked about the print media or radio,

2412
06:13:10,709 --> 06:13:15,290
and its issue with gender stereotypes.

2413
06:13:15,590 --> 06:13:24,569
I would like to ask Ministry of Culture and Commission of Communication to talk about the media.

2414
06:13:24,869 --> 06:13:31,389
And finally, you talk about post-sexual assault and the monitoring and follow-up,

2415
06:13:32,489 --> 06:13:36,930
and the indictment and judicial processing.

2416
06:13:37,310 --> 06:13:44,669
We will give the floor to Judicial Yuan before we give the floor to the Ministry of Justice.

2417
06:13:44,909 --> 06:13:46,830
That will be more appropriate.

2418
06:13:47,490 --> 06:13:51,569
So that's the order of the answering later on.

2419
06:13:52,750 --> 06:13:56,270
And so that was the Ministry of Labor.

2420
06:13:56,470 --> 06:13:58,290
We next give the floor to Ministry of Education.

2421
06:14:00,010 --> 06:14:03,270
And this is Ministry of Education.

2422
06:14:03,369 --> 06:14:09,470
So in 2023, we actually amended the three acts regarding gender equality.

2423
06:14:09,610 --> 06:14:15,470
So after the amendment, should there be sexual harassment on campus,

2424
06:14:15,630 --> 06:14:23,450
then we would actually address all these cases by using Gender Equity Education Act.

2425
06:14:23,450 --> 06:14:28,369
