06:57:30,889 --> 06:57:42,729
So I think I will call on Professor Letty to take questions on article seven and eight so that we can try to make up for time.

2628
06:57:43,389 --> 06:57:46,389
And then the delegation can respond to all those questions.

2629
06:57:46,669 --> 06:57:48,529
Thank you very much for your questions.

2630
06:57:50,130 --> 06:57:50,689
Thank you, Sher.

2631
06:57:52,489 --> 06:58:03,790
During our chair's remarks on article four, some questions regarding political participation were already addressed.

2632
06:58:04,509 --> 06:58:08,189
However, I would like to emphasize some points.

2633
06:58:09,190 --> 06:58:20,189
First, what is the state party doing to address all topics contained in general recommendation 40, especially?

2634
06:58:21,110 --> 06:58:33,549
Is there a commitment from political parties to comply with party rules and to foster a greater presence of women in the public sphere?

2635
06:58:35,110 --> 06:58:45,069
Could the state party provide more information on the participation of these advantage groups in public life?

2636
06:58:45,729 --> 06:59:03,209
Please provide data and information on the participation of rural women, indigenous women, women with disabilities, LGBT persons and other marginalized groups in political and public life.

2637
06:59:03,209 --> 06:59:15,889
Are indigenous and rural women and women with disabilities participating in public consultation regarding decisions that affect them?

2638
06:59:15,889 --> 06:59:43,029
In light of reports of increasing harassment and gender-based violence against women in public life, including online violence, please provide information on measures taken to prevent and address harassment, hate speech and cyber violence targeting women in politics.

2639
06:59:43,029 --> 06:59:54,950
Are there specific ways to report political violence against women an effective way to sanction it?

2640
06:59:54,950 --> 07:00:18,490
About article eight, my question is, please describe measures taken to promote women's leadership in international representation, including mentorship, career advancement and visibility of women role models.

2641
07:00:19,090 --> 07:00:19,790
Thank you, Sher.

2642
07:00:22,169 --> 07:00:23,369
Thank you very much.

2643
07:00:23,470 --> 07:00:32,610
I will now hand back to the delegation to try and in a short way respond to questions for article six.

2644
07:00:32,729 --> 07:00:37,369
I think there were four of them, and the questions are on article seven and eight.

2645
07:00:37,450 --> 07:00:37,790
Thank you.

2646
07:00:42,509 --> 07:00:43,770
Thank you very much.

2647
07:00:43,770 --> 07:01:10,069
Regarding article six and regarding the sanctions about or penalizing women in sex work, we will have the Ministry of Justice answer and the Ministry of Interior to follow up.

2648
07:01:10,069 --> 07:01:27,750
And then regarding comfort women, whether or not there is going to be a dedicated national women or gender museum, we will give this question to the Ministry of Health and Welfare and then have NGOs follow up.

2649
07:01:27,750 --> 07:01:35,729
And we will have the Ministry of Culture to take up the question about the textbook in article six.

2650
07:01:35,889 --> 07:01:44,549
That's about article six and about article seven, investing in women participation by political parties.

2651
07:01:45,770 --> 07:01:53,770
And for the participation of disadvantaged women, we will give this question to Ministry of Interior.

2652
07:01:53,770 --> 07:02:10,889
And regarding the sexual harassment online and offline, politically targeting women, we will give this question to the Ministry of Justice and international participation.

2653
07:02:10,990 --> 07:02:15,130
We will give the question to Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

2654
07:02:15,409 --> 07:02:16,529
That's for article eight.

2655
07:02:17,409 --> 07:02:20,430
Now we give the floor to the respective delegates.

2656
07:02:20,669 --> 07:02:21,610
Please mind the time.

2657
07:02:21,610 --> 07:02:22,610
Thank you.

2658
07:02:26,889 --> 07:02:37,189
Minister of Interior, police agency regarding article six about sexual transaction.

2659
07:02:37,189 --> 07:03:00,270
In 2009, the interpretation gave way to the Public Order Act in Taiwan, and because of the social consensus in Taiwan and the Zoning Act in Taiwan in the past,

2660
07:03:00,270 --> 07:03:17,450
Keelung, Zhanghua and Jiayi had evaluated whether or not we were going to establish a zone for sexual work and sex service work, but there were no consensus.

2661
07:03:17,450 --> 07:03:27,330
So because of the limitation in the legislation, we've adjusted in our implementation.

2662
07:03:27,330 --> 07:03:41,610
In the past, we focused more on article 231 in our code.

2663
07:03:41,610 --> 07:03:57,650
And we noticed that for these economic pinpoints, if we do not cut it, cut off from the start.

2664
07:03:57,650 --> 07:04:16,810
And we followed up from, we tracked from the bottom up and combining forces that are non-police and work with local governments, industry, constructions, engineering,

2665
07:04:16,810 --> 07:04:40,830
and using the building code and the fire agency codes to cut the power and water of these illegal sex service stations, we can break these organized crimes of sex trafficking.

2666
07:04:40,830 --> 07:04:52,150
And for those that are the individual sex service providers, we work with social services and labor and police.

2667
07:04:52,709 --> 07:05:07,950
After we finish the police statement, we will give them access to social welfare or other accesses.

2668
07:05:07,950 --> 07:05:17,349
And if they have these requirements in five days, we will have a confidential letter that will be sent to them.

2669
07:05:18,189 --> 07:05:28,409
And there will be a green channel provided for this individual to leave, exit the sex service.

2670
07:05:28,409 --> 07:05:35,150
And we also work with CSOs to provide follow-up care.

2671
07:05:36,490 --> 07:05:39,009
What about Ministry of Justice?

2672
07:05:40,010 --> 07:05:43,090
This is the Ministry of Justice.

2673
07:05:43,849 --> 07:05:56,930
And regarding penalizing the sex service providing, if it's a broker or seductive transactions,

2674
07:05:56,930 --> 07:06:13,029
we can see in our criminal code Article 231 to 233 in our Human Trafficking Prevention Act Article 29, there are no penalization.

2675
07:06:14,750 --> 07:06:29,430
And secondly is from the comfort women to gender and human rights museum,

2676
07:06:29,930 --> 07:06:35,630
we give this question to Ministry of Health and Welfare, Ministry of Culture, and Ministry of Education.

2677
07:06:35,630 --> 07:06:43,610
This is the Ministry of Health and Welfare regarding the social services provided to comfort women.

2678
07:06:44,849 --> 07:07:00,090
We have already a program that provides consultation and subsidy to comfort women that provided service during the Japanese colony,

2679
07:07:00,189 --> 07:07:03,529
and we have allowances provided in medical services.

2680
07:07:03,529 --> 07:07:10,990
This program ended as the last comfort women passed away in 2023.

2681
07:07:13,349 --> 07:07:23,790
But before this, we provided these services to them, and I now give the floor to Ministry of Culture.

2682
07:07:26,009 --> 07:07:34,450
The museum falls under the jurisdiction of Ministry of Culture, so I think you can take this question together.

2683
07:07:37,450 --> 07:07:42,689
A museum falls under the jurisdiction of Ministry of Culture,

2684
07:07:42,689 --> 07:07:57,430
but in terms of women rescue and social welfare that falls under the jurisdiction of Ministry of Health and Welfare,

2685
07:07:57,770 --> 07:08:07,270
I would like to say that the government is more than willing to work with SCSO to partner in promoting a very important task,

2686
07:08:07,270 --> 07:08:15,049
but we know it takes cross-department work to further facilitate this.

2687
07:08:15,729 --> 07:08:35,150
For the Ministry of Culture, we should first work with the SCSO to foster environments like the touring museums before we build something that's permanent.

2688
07:08:35,150 --> 07:08:46,389
We need to take this issue into schools, into communities for the public to gain access to this part of the history.

2689
07:08:46,389 --> 07:08:54,569
So since 2016 to 2026, this year for the past decade, at the Ministry of Culture,

2690
07:08:55,029 --> 07:09:05,470
we have invested in over $23 million for SCSOs to advocate this issue,

2691
07:09:05,470 --> 07:09:16,790
including 814 International Comfort Women Day or concerts or film festivals or art performances,

2692
07:09:17,450 --> 07:09:24,330
various activities to raise the awareness among the general public and to know the value of this part of the history.

2693
07:09:24,330 --> 07:09:42,750
And we know that we also helped the AMA Museum in improving the accessible infrastructures, their curations, exhibitions.

2694
07:09:42,930 --> 07:09:47,270
I don't think we need to wait for a museum to be built.

2695
07:09:47,270 --> 07:09:54,849
There are already a lot of things that we can work with them, but if we need to build a museum,

2696
07:09:55,069 --> 07:09:59,990
we need the Compton Authority to take up this responsibility.

2697
07:10:00,529 --> 07:10:05,590
We would like to give the floor to the Ministry of Education for the textbook and curriculum.

2698
07:10:06,590 --> 07:10:19,930
Regarding the curriculum, it covers the 20th century history suffered by people in East Asia,

2699
07:10:20,529 --> 07:10:23,409
and it includes gender and history.

2700
07:10:23,810 --> 07:10:30,189
In terms of human rights and education, it's also an important issue in the curriculum.

2701
07:10:30,189 --> 07:10:40,250
Teachers can guide students to reflect on humanity and dignity

2702
07:10:41,190 --> 07:10:50,610
and think about how bias and discrimination affects equality.

2703
07:10:51,610 --> 07:11:01,729
These are all resources that we dedicated in our Gender Equality Education Resource Center.

2704
07:11:03,590 --> 07:11:13,049
And we also have a thematic case on women treatment in war.

2705
07:11:13,049 --> 07:11:21,950
All of this are placed in our Gender Resource Center for teachers to download and use in class.

2706
07:11:24,470 --> 07:11:25,330
Thank you very much.

2707
07:11:26,290 --> 07:11:32,110
Next, we move on to Article 7 about encouraging female political participation.

2708
07:11:32,349 --> 07:11:34,209
We now give the floor to MOI.

2709
07:11:35,209 --> 07:11:45,130
Regarding support or encourage political parties to foster female political participation,

2710
07:11:46,409 --> 07:11:56,630
in the last legislative session, EY submitted to the LY an amendment to encourage political parties

2711
07:11:56,630 --> 07:12:05,630
to use 5% of their political party's subsidy to empower and facilitate female participation.

2712
07:12:06,750 --> 07:12:14,189
But last year, because the legislative session did not continue, we weren't able to review that and adopt that.

2713
07:12:14,209 --> 07:12:18,750
But in the future, if it's adopted, 5% will be allocated to it.

2714
07:12:18,750 --> 07:12:21,889
Right now, because the amendment hasn't been adopted,

2715
07:12:22,310 --> 07:12:30,509
we will continue to encourage and raise the awareness of female participation in political parties.

2716
07:12:30,590 --> 07:12:38,790
And we remind the political parties to use a certain ratio of their political party subsidy

2717
07:12:38,790 --> 07:12:44,229
to encourage or facilitate female political participation.

2718
07:12:44,229 --> 07:12:49,709
And also, when these political parties are holding their annual assemblies,

2719
07:12:49,970 --> 07:13:02,490
we take part and we notify them that there should be a certain ratio allocated for women and women with disabilities.

2720
07:13:03,509 --> 07:13:11,930
And there are voluntary quotas for these political parties as well.

2721
07:13:11,930 --> 07:13:20,229
For example, the ruling party, the DPP, we ask that various companies and various sectors,

2722
07:13:20,830 --> 07:13:30,270
in addition to the candidates that they have, out of every four candidates, there should be one female.

2723
07:13:30,689 --> 07:13:37,709
So we should make sure that this guarantees the female participation ratio.

2724
07:13:37,709 --> 07:13:49,029
But we did notice that in rural areas and counties and townships, this ratio wasn't adhered to.

2725
07:13:49,290 --> 07:13:58,450
So we actively negotiated with the legislators and amended Article 33 of the Local Administrative Act

2726
07:13:58,450 --> 07:14:04,909
and changed the one-third ratio to one out of every four.

2727
07:14:05,909 --> 07:14:14,090
And it will start applying in 2030, which means during the next election.

2728
07:14:14,490 --> 07:14:22,970
And after that, we will have twice the amount of guaranteed seats for women.

2729
07:14:24,849 --> 07:14:30,849
Sexual violence and also the sexual violence targeting political participating women.

2730
07:14:30,849 --> 07:14:34,930
So this is from the Department of the Ministry of Justice.

2731
07:14:35,229 --> 07:14:41,930
So for a female politician being targeted by hate crime, hate cybercrime,

2732
07:14:42,169 --> 07:14:49,770
and also that constitutes a sexual harassment act violation,

2733
07:14:50,110 --> 07:14:54,150
and then they can actually prosecute according to these acts.

2734
07:14:54,189 --> 07:14:55,729
So these are my answers.

2735
07:14:55,729 --> 07:14:57,189
Thank you very much.

2736
07:14:57,270 --> 07:15:00,790
Article 8 about this international political participation.

2737
07:15:00,950 --> 07:15:03,009
I would like to give the floor to MOFA.

2738
07:15:04,930 --> 07:15:09,490
I'm with the Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

2739
07:15:10,189 --> 07:15:15,189
I would like to use Taiwan's women's participation in AIPAC as an example

2740
07:15:15,189 --> 07:15:20,610
for Taiwan's progress in promoting women's international participation.

2741
07:15:20,610 --> 07:15:27,610
Among the members of Taiwan's delegation to the 2024 AIPAC economic leaders meeting,

2742
07:15:28,729 --> 07:15:34,369
women accounted for 42 percent, up to 40 percent in 2020.

2743
07:15:35,310 --> 07:15:40,209
Women also played an active role in AIPAC meetings throughout the year.

2744
07:15:40,209 --> 07:15:50,770
In 2024, Taiwan sent a total of 504 experts from government and private sector in AIPAC meetings,

2745
07:15:51,529 --> 07:15:55,970
and women made up to 52 percent of the participation.

2746
07:15:56,490 --> 07:16:01,909
This means that the female participation was higher than male participation overall.

2747
07:16:01,909 --> 07:16:11,810
In addition, four women from Taiwan hold key positions in various AIPAC forums in 2024,

2748
07:16:12,470 --> 07:16:16,509
representing 30 percent of all such positions held by Taiwan.

2749
07:16:17,029 --> 07:16:21,909
This includes the Chair of Agricultural Technical Cooperation Working Group,

2750
07:16:22,970 --> 07:16:31,009
ATCWG, also the Vice Governor of the Security and Trust Steering Group, STSG, and so on.

2751
07:16:31,009 --> 07:16:38,470
So these figures demonstrate Taiwan's continued effort to promote women's international participation.

2752
07:16:38,689 --> 07:16:40,150
Thank you.

2753
07:16:45,630 --> 07:16:53,810
Do we have any other colleagues who would like to answer or provide additional information to these articles?

2754
07:16:54,509 --> 07:17:00,430
None? If not, then we are going to give the floor back

2755
07:17:00,430 --> 07:17:02,490
to our review committee.

2756
07:17:02,630 --> 07:17:04,310
Thank you.

2757
07:17:07,590 --> 07:17:08,049
Thank you.

2758
07:17:08,330 --> 07:17:10,130
You just want to repeat the question?

2759
07:17:12,169 --> 07:17:16,549
Because I didn't get the answer to my question to the Ministry of Interior,

2760
07:17:17,770 --> 07:17:22,689
who answered about your criminal code Article 231,

2761
07:17:22,689 --> 07:17:31,930
but there was no reply to my question on what happened to the research report.

2762
07:17:32,549 --> 07:17:40,349
And then after that, what kind of action was taken, especially regarding decriminalization?

2763
07:17:40,590 --> 07:17:49,849
And although you said that criminal code Article 231, 233 is about trafficking-related forcing, et cetera,

2764
07:17:49,849 --> 07:18:01,549
but what about Public Order Maintenance Act, Article 80, which punishes sexual transaction?

2765
07:18:02,169 --> 07:18:06,209
And that's mostly by that law that women are punished with fine.

2766
07:18:07,990 --> 07:18:09,049
Thank you very much.

2767
07:18:09,209 --> 07:18:16,470
I think while we await the response to that, I will give the floor to Marion for questions on Article 9.

2768
07:18:16,569 --> 07:18:17,290
Thank you.

2769
07:18:18,290 --> 07:18:20,009
Thank you, Madam Chair.

2770
07:18:20,810 --> 07:18:23,990
Yes, so this addresses nationality issues.

2771
07:18:24,590 --> 07:18:29,349
The committee notes with appreciation the information provided by the State Party,

2772
07:18:29,709 --> 07:18:36,169
indicating that naturalization applications are no longer rejected disproportionately for women

2773
07:18:36,169 --> 07:18:41,729
on the basis of the quotation, no illicit or illegal behavior criterion,

2774
07:18:41,729 --> 07:18:47,590
and that objective regulations have been adopted to clarify these applications.

2775
07:18:48,330 --> 07:18:53,009
Nevertheless, the committee recalls that concerns raised during the previous review

2776
07:18:53,009 --> 07:18:58,209
extended beyond the interpretation of this criterion and related more broadly

2777
07:18:58,209 --> 07:19:03,650
to the equal enjoyment of nationality rights by new immigrant women.

2778
07:19:04,389 --> 07:19:11,029
Can the delegation elaborate on how the implementation of the revised Nationality Act

2779
07:19:11,029 --> 07:19:16,470
is being monitored to ensure that the no illicit or illegal behavior criterion

2780
07:19:16,470 --> 07:19:21,610
is applied consistently and without direct or indirect discrimination?

2781
07:19:22,310 --> 07:19:28,189
Furthermore, what mechanisms are available to monitor the practical impact of these reforms,

2782
07:19:28,869 --> 07:19:32,810
including access to effective remedies where applications are refused?

2783
07:19:33,790 --> 07:19:38,029
The committee also welcomes the various empowerment programs, educational initiatives,

2784
07:19:38,290 --> 07:19:43,029
and psychosocial support services available to new immigrant women.

2785
07:19:44,049 --> 07:19:48,610
Can the delegation indicate how the effectiveness of these programs is assessed

2786
07:19:48,610 --> 07:19:53,529
and whether they have resulted in measurable improvements in the economic independence,

2787
07:19:54,270 --> 07:19:58,150
social participation, and long-term integration of new immigrant women,

2788
07:19:58,409 --> 07:20:03,270
particularly those living in rural areas or experiencing multiple forms of discrimination?

2789
07:20:04,170 --> 07:20:07,750
In regard to residence rights and family unity,

2790
07:20:08,389 --> 07:20:12,529
the committee welcomes the 2023 amendment to the Immigration Act,

2791
07:20:12,909 --> 07:20:16,830
which expands residence rights for certain categories of new immigrants,

2792
07:20:17,569 --> 07:20:23,950
including those whose spouse has died or those maintaining custody or regular contact with their children.

2793
07:20:24,770 --> 07:20:28,650
However, the committee recalls that concerns were previously expressed

2794
07:20:28,650 --> 07:20:32,450
regarding the residency rights of divorced migrant spouses

2795
07:20:32,450 --> 07:20:38,189
and the possible impact of immigration rules on women's autonomy and parental rights.

2796
07:20:39,029 --> 07:20:45,169
Can the delegation update the committee on any follow-up to the study on residency and parental rights

2797
07:20:45,169 --> 07:20:48,450
of divorced new immigrants, including its principal findings

2798
07:20:49,009 --> 07:20:53,470
and the manner in which these have informed legislative or policy reforms?

2799
07:20:54,250 --> 07:20:58,830
In addition, what measures are being taken to ensure that women's residence status

2800
07:20:58,830 --> 07:21:03,630
is not dependent upon remaining in abusive or coercive relationships

2801
07:21:03,630 --> 07:21:06,610
and that the best interests of children are fully protected?

2802
07:21:08,090 --> 07:21:10,529
In regard to nationality rights of children,

2803
07:21:11,009 --> 07:21:16,610
the committee welcomes the amendments adopted to facilitate the naturalization of stateless children

2804
07:21:16,610 --> 07:21:20,750
and notes the progress reported by the State Party in this regard.

2805
07:21:21,569 --> 07:21:27,250
Nevertheless, questions remain regarding the equal enjoyment of family rights by all children,

2806
07:21:27,250 --> 07:21:30,290
particularly those growing up in diverse family structures.

2807
07:21:31,130 --> 07:21:36,270
The committee has received information indicating that despite the legalization of same-sex marriage,

2808
07:21:36,630 --> 07:21:41,349
children born within same-sex marriages through assisted reproductive technologies

2809
07:21:41,349 --> 07:21:44,250
may still face unequal recognition of parentage,

2810
07:21:44,930 --> 07:21:48,529
requiring one parent to establish legal parentage through adoption

2811
07:21:48,529 --> 07:21:54,150
rather than benefiting from the same legal presumption applicable to different sex-married couples.

2812
07:21:54,150 --> 07:21:59,869
Can the delegation explain whether consideration is being given

2813
07:21:59,869 --> 07:22:03,590
to reviewing the existing legal framework governing parentage

2814
07:22:03,590 --> 07:22:09,810
in order to ensure equal protection of all children, irrespective of sex or sexual orientation?

2815
07:22:11,270 --> 07:22:15,029
Finally, the committee notes that Taiwan has made important progress

2816
07:22:15,029 --> 07:22:19,849
in strengthening the legal and policy framework governing nationality, migration,

2817
07:22:19,970 --> 07:22:21,930
and the protection of new immigrant women.

2818
07:22:21,930 --> 07:22:28,110
However, many of the measures described appear to rely primarily on administrative programs

2819
07:22:28,110 --> 07:22:29,950
and policy initiatives.

2820
07:22:30,490 --> 07:22:36,130
Can the delegation explain what steps are being taken to ensure the long-term sustainability

2821
07:22:36,130 --> 07:22:38,950
and institutionalization of these measures,

2822
07:22:39,549 --> 07:22:42,970
including whether they are supported by binding legislative frameworks,

2823
07:22:43,750 --> 07:22:49,529
dedicated budgetary allocations, and effective monitoring and accountability mechanisms?

2824
07:22:50,529 --> 07:22:51,849
Thank you, Madam Chair.

2825
07:22:54,770 --> 07:22:55,750
Thank you very much.

2826
07:22:55,930 --> 07:23:03,009
Now I will turn over to the delegation for if possible short answers.

2827
07:23:03,590 --> 07:23:06,810
Thank you.

2828
07:23:10,409 --> 07:23:15,130
So without this Article 80 of the Social Order Maintaining Act,

2829
07:23:15,130 --> 07:23:21,610
so we would like to ask the Ministry of Interior to take that as to the nationality,

2830
07:23:21,709 --> 07:23:24,349
especially the naturalization of citizenship.

2831
07:23:24,430 --> 07:23:27,930
These are relevant to the new immigrants.

2832
07:23:28,330 --> 07:23:36,150
And then the new immigrants' treatment, I think it's relevant to the immigration office.

2833
07:23:36,389 --> 07:23:40,669
So we would like to ask the Ministry of Interior to take that question.

2834
07:23:40,669 --> 07:23:48,150
And as to the immigration and migrant workers, their undocumented children and their children's protection,

2835
07:23:48,650 --> 07:23:53,869
maybe the Ministry of Labor can take that question by providing additional information.

2836
07:23:54,450 --> 07:24:04,650
And also, same-sex marriage, the presumption of parentage protection,

2837
07:24:04,650 --> 07:24:16,450
I think for these parental law, can we ask the Ministry of Justice to take this question?

2838
07:24:18,909 --> 07:24:23,990
And also these non-citizen children's protection,

2839
07:24:25,889 --> 07:24:31,549
I think that we can ask Ministry of Interior, Ministry of Education,

2840
07:24:31,549 --> 07:24:34,590
and Ministry of Health and Welfare to take the question.

2841
07:24:34,830 --> 07:24:39,810
So we would like to ask these colleagues to get ready to answer this question

2842
07:24:39,810 --> 07:24:43,869
